					<description><![CDATA[<p>In this post, we take a look at the AllAboutFPL's FPL GW1 Scout Picks team, which is based on form, stats, eye-test, and analysis.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/fpl-gw1-scout-picks-based-on-stats-analysis-and-matchups/">FPL GW1 Scout Picks Based on Stats, Analysis and Matchups</a> appeared first on <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com">ALLABOUTFPL: Your one stop place for all FPL tips, FPL captain picks, FPL news, FPL players, previews, reviews,differential picks, analysis and weekly updates.</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Welcome to our <strong>FPL GW1 Scout Picks blog!</strong> We&#8217;re back! It&#8217;s that time again &#8211; with the new Premier League season now just days away it is time for the final changes, the last bits of tinkering and the flip-flopping to stop. Having drafted, re-drafted, and then gone back to the initial draft time and time again, it is time to make a decision and finalise our teams for FPL GW1.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Every week we will bring you a team of 11 players that we think will be high scoring asset &#8211; sometimes we&#8217;re wrong, sometimes we&#8217;re right, but we always explain our picks in detail. Whether you are a new reader, or a Scout Picks veteran, I hope you find this series insightful and helpful throughout the season.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">As always, our Scout Picks will be based on the eye test, stats, analysis and in this case also Pre-Season. Let&#8217;s first take a look at the <strong>fixtures for FPL GW1</strong>.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/category/ultimate-2026-27-fpl-pre-season-guide/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/category/ultimate-2026-27-fpl-pre-season-guide/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color"><strong>Link to all our 2026/27 Pre-Season articles</strong></mark></a> including all team pre-season friendly updates, best drafts, fixture analysis, position-wise analysis, differentials, players to target, budget enablers and more. Completely free to access as well!</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center">FPL GW1 Fixtures</h2>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1024" height="793" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.10.16-1024x793.png" alt="FPL GW1 fixtures" class="wp-image-84961" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.10.16-1024x793.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.10.16-300x232.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.10.16-768x594.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.10.16-1536x1189.png 1536w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.10.16-600x464.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.10.16.png 1876w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read: </strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/top-mid-priced-premium-fpl-forwards6-0-for-2026-27-season/"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Top Mid Priced &amp; Premium FPL Forwards(&gt;6.0) for 2026/27 season</mark></strong></a></p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center">FPL GW1 Scout Picks</h2>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">FPL GW1 Scout Picks &#8211; Goalkeeper</h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="193" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.11-1024x193.png" alt="FPL GW1 Scout Picks - Goalkeeper" class="wp-image-84962" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.11-1024x193.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.11-300x57.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.11-768x145.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.11-1536x290.png 1536w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.11-600x113.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.11.png 1876w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Kinsky</strong> (4.5m) is our FPL GW1 Scout Picks goalkeeper due to his affordability, security of minutes and fixture. Spurs finished last season in 17th just two points above relegated West Ham thanks to a final day victory against Everton. Had things gone differently, De Zerbi&#8217;s side may well have been playing championship football this weekend, but instead their goalkeeper is our pick for FPL GW1 Scout Picks &#8211; let me explain&#8230;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>FACT: Between De Zerbi&#8217;s appointment in GW32 and the end of the season, Spurs had the best (lowest) xGA in the league.</strong></p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-116-1024x1024.png" alt="Goalkeeper Rotation FPL" class="wp-image-84979" style="width:618px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-116-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-116-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-116-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-116-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-116-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-116.png 1080w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Spurs are generally considered to be a decent side, with a good manager and a largely overhauled squad from the one that almost got them relegated last season. <strong>Their defence has been massively improved with the additions of Senesi, Van Hecke and Robertson</strong>, while their midfield has been radically altered by the club record purchases of Tonali and Fernandes. While their attack could still do with a bit of work, the foundations of a good side are there. Furthermore, De Zerbi is a capable, forward thinking coach who showed last season that he can get a tune out of these players.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Considering that many are tipping Spurs to end up in and around the top 6 places yet again this season, Kinsky represents excellent value as a 4.5m starting goalkeeper. Brentford away is by no means an easy game, but <strong>Spurs managed to limit opposing sides to less than 1xG worth of chances in 3 of their 5 final premier league games</strong>. Spurs conceded the <strong>third fewest goals in the league from De Zerbi&#8217;s appointment to the end of the season </strong>&#8211; a fact which illustrates how effective the new manager is at coaching a stubborn defensive unit (contrary to popular belief).</p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Fantasy Football Hub(FFHUB)</mark></a></strong></p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full is-resized"><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1000" height="596" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_MoneyBack_1000x596.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84100" style="width:768px;height:undefinedpx" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_MoneyBack_1000x596.png 1000w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_MoneyBack_1000x596-300x179.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_MoneyBack_1000x596-768x458.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_MoneyBack_1000x596-600x358.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px" /></a><figcaption class="wp-element-caption"><strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Fantasy Football Hub</mark></a></strong> is a high-quality FPL website offering a wide range of FPL content, tools, data, planners, and more. Memberships are available for the 2026/27 season at a <strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><mark><mark style="background-color:#ffffff" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">50% discount</mark></mark></a></strong> along with a win-your-mini-league or get-your-money-back guarantee<strong>(<a href="https://www.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/terms-and-conditions" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">T&amp;C Applicable</mark></a>).</strong> (Click on the image above to claim the offer)</figcaption></figure>
</div>


<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">FPL GW1 Scout Picks &#8211; Defenders</h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="170" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.23-1024x170.png" alt="FPL GW1 Scout Picks - Defenders" class="wp-image-84963" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.23-1024x170.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.23-300x50.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.23-768x128.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.23-1536x255.png 1536w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.23-600x100.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.23.png 1876w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Calafiori</strong> (5.5m), <strong>Mosquera</strong> (5.5m) and <strong>Maguire</strong> (5.0m) make up our backline for FPL GW1&#8230;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Arsenal were by far the best defence in the league last season, and with a fixture against a promoted sign at the Emirates in FPL GW1 it makes sense to go all in on their defensive assets from the get-go. With Gabriel coming in at an eye-watering 8.0m this year, we&#8217;ve decided to select the cheaper options of <strong>Calafiori</strong> and <strong>Mosquera</strong> to start the season. Our thought process here is to go for nailed Arsenal defenders, and as <strong>both of these guys started the Community Shield against Manchester City</strong> last weekend, it looks like they&#8217;re set to start in FPL GW1 also.</p>


<img decoding="async" src="https://thumbs.smartframe.io/04742eb90cefa12a5e3ab9bae92c2b93/neim5Foe0TYf.webp?force-scraper=rss&#038;t=rss" alt="SmartFrame Image" />


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Calafiori actually had the second most points-per-game of any Arsenal defender</strong> (100+ minutes) last season, beaten only by Gabriel in that regard &#8211; but the issue was his availability, playing just 22 for the gunners in their 25/26 title winning campaign. Calafiori proved to be a nailed asset and a reliable source of points when fit, but failed to stay fit for long enough to become a real FPL gem. <strong>The Italian&#8217;s DEFCON potential is limited, averaging just 5.41 CBIT/90 last season</strong>, but it is his attacking output that sets him apart from his peers. As evidenced by his exciting display (and goal) against City in the community shield, Calafiori is given license to get up the pitch and help out in the final third when possible, making him an appealing FPL asset.</p>



<p class="has-text-align-left wp-block-paragraph"><strong>FACT: Arsenal conceded just 27 goals and 33.1xGA last season!</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Our second Arsenal defender is <strong>Mosquera</strong>, who has become a popular pick due to<strong> Saliba&#8217;s injury </strong>&#8211; though it must be mentioned that Arsenal remain in the hunt for another centre back, a scenario which could push Mosquera out of the starting line-up. As things stand, however, <strong>Mosquera offers another cheap way into an Arsenal backline</strong> that proved to be a reliable source of clean sheet points last season &#8211; with the Gunners ending the season with a massive 19 clean sheets. <strong>Mosquera averaged 8.40 CBIT/90 last season in his limited game time</strong>, but this will likely decrease with more time spent on the pitch (he was often coming on late on in games to sure up the backline and was therefore a more active defender thus higher CBIT). With two Arsenal defenders we hope to effectively cover for Gabriel&#8217;s potential hauls, and with a very good fixture in GW1, it makes sense to target Arsenal anyway!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Completing the backline is Manchester United&#8217;s <strong>Maguire</strong>. United&#8217;s defensive assets have been talked up throughout much of pre-season due to their attractive first two fixtures against two promoted sides in<strong> Ipswich and Hull</strong>. Going into a new season it&#8217;s very hard to predict which fixtures should be targeted, especially with so many new managers in the league, and thus attacking the promoted sides early on is a safe strategy.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-123-1024x1024.png" alt="Maguire FPL" class="wp-image-84990" style="width:613px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-123-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-123-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-123-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-123-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-123-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-123.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption"><strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/fpl-rotational-pairs-combinations-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/fpl-rotational-pairs-combinations-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">5 Defender and Budget Midfielder Rotation from our Rotational Pairs and Combinations article</mark></a></strong></figcaption></figure>
</div>


<p class="has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph"><strong>FACT: From Carrick&#8217;s appointment to the end of the season, Manchester United picked up the most points in the league.</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Carrick&#8217;s side ended the season well and saw an uptick in both their attacking and defensive numbers under the new manager&#8217;s stewardship. <strong>Maguire&#8217;s season CBIT/90 average was around 8, but that figure jumped up to 9.48CBIT/90 during the final 8 games </strong>of the season. Shaw&#8217;s numbers also increased in this time, hinting at a system change and more active defensive roles for United&#8217;s backline. <strong>Shaw should be considered for our teams as he represents great value at just 4.5m,</strong> but Maguire is a better FPL asset due to his elevated goal threat and DC potential.</p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Fantasy Football Hub(FFHUB) Free AI Team Rating Tool</mark></a></strong></p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1000" height="596" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84095" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596.png 1000w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596-300x179.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596-768x458.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596-600x358.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px" /></a><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Get your team rated by <strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" data-type="link" data-id="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Fantasy Football Hub</mark></a></strong>&#8216;s AI Team Rating tool for free (Click on the image above to get your team rated).</figcaption></figure>
</div>


<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">FPL GW1 Scout Picks &#8211; Midfielders</h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="172" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.32-1024x172.png" alt="FPL GW1 Scout Picks - Midfielders" class="wp-image-84964" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.32-1024x172.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.32-300x50.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.32-768x129.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.32-1536x258.png 1536w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.32-600x101.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.32.png 1856w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We&#8217;ve selected a midfield four of <strong>Mbeumo</strong> (8.0m), <strong>Fernandes</strong> (12.0m), <strong>Szoboszlai</strong> (7.0m) and <strong>Tzolis</strong> (6.5m) for FPL GW1&#8230;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">As mentioned in the defenders section, due to a lack of data the safest fixtures to target are the promoted teams and therefore United look like a very attractive proposition in FPL GW1. <strong>Bruno Fernandes is pretty much essential for these first two GWs</strong>, and we&#8217;ve decided to double up with Mbeumo also in our FPL GW1 scout picks team.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Last year <strong>Bruno scored 9 goals and provided 21 assists in the league, averaging a goal involvement every 102 minutes.</strong> It may surprise some to discover that Bruno over performed his underlying assist data last season &#8211; his 17.8xA is some 3xA under his actual tally (though he did under perform his xG by almost 3). <strong>Last season was undoubtedly the most creative campaign</strong> of his career, but the underlying numbers suggest it wasn&#8217;t entirely out of nowhere. His numbers were up on his United career average of 0.34xG/90 and 0.32xA/90 (0.66xGI/90 compared to last season’s 0.87xGI/90). </p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="858" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-18-at-13.35.45-1024x858.png" alt="Bruno Fernandes FPL" class="wp-image-84987" style="width:617px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-18-at-13.35.45-1024x858.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-18-at-13.35.45-300x251.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-18-at-13.35.45-768x644.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-18-at-13.35.45-600x503.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-18-at-13.35.45.png 1050w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph"><strong>FACT: Bruno produced 10 goal involvements in Manchester United&#8217;s final 10 Premier League fixtures.</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Bruno was taking fewer but far more valuable shots (xG wise) last season compared to previous seasons,</strong> averaging an xG/shot of 0.14 compared to the previous season’s 0.1. Since joining Manchester United Bruno has been taking fewer shots but creating more chances, illustrated by a sharp drop off in his Sh90 and a steady increase in both his KP90 over his time in Red. We could say, therefore, that Bruno is just continuing on this career trajectory, and that last season was a demonstration of the player he has become during his time at Manchester United (<strong>more creative, fewer shots</strong>). Fundamentally Bruno is a fantastic FPL asset even at his elevated price-tag and in my opinion he&#8217;s a must have for the first two GWs.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We&#8217;ve gone for the United double-up in GW1, with <strong>Mbeumo</strong> also selected for the FPL GW1 Scout Picks team due to the fact that he will be playing as an <strong>out-of-position striker and is priced as a 8.0m midfielder in FPL.</strong> Mbeumo scored <strong>11 goals and provided 3 assists last season, averaging 0.45xG/90 and 0.17xA/90 (0.62xGI/90)</strong>. Though he was outshone somewhat by Sesko and Cunha towards the end of the season, his underlying numbers actually saw an uptick under Carrick. In fact, <strong>Mbeumo had by far the highest xG/90 of any player (1000+ minutes) to play under Carrick</strong> at Manchester United, a stat which shows how critical he was to their attack.</p>


<img decoding="async" src="https://thumbs.smartframe.io/04742eb90cefa12a5e3ab9bae92c2b93/ARCH796487_00356467.webp?force-scraper=rss&#038;t=rss" alt="SmartFrame Image" />


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Mbeumo ranks top for xG/90 amongst the semi-premium mids (7.0-8.5m midfielders)</strong> and second only to Cherki for xGI/90. Where he falls down, unfortunately, is his xG underperformance. Unlike many of the other players in this list Mbeumo actually underperformed his xG last season by about 2 goals &#8211; this may not sound like much but an additional 10 points in FPL across the course of a season can make all the difference to final rank! That being said, if you’re looking for a <strong>high upside attacker with great initial fixtures</strong> then Mbeumo is a great asset for FPL GW1.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Mbeumo in pre-season: <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/26bd.png" alt="⚽" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/26bd.png" alt="⚽" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/26bd.png" alt="⚽" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f170.png" alt="🅰" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /></strong> (<strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-27-pre-season-summary-of-all-20-premier-league-teams/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-27-pre-season-summary-of-all-20-premier-league-teams/"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Full Pre- Season Summary of all 20 Teams here</mark></a></strong>)</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Szoboszlai</strong> is another popular semi-premium midfielder, coming in at just 7.0m in FPL this year. Liverpool really underwhelmed last season but there is much more optimism around the club this year thanks in large part to the appointment of new manager Iraola (formerly of Bournemouth). Iraola will look to set Liverpool up in a 4-2-3-1 playing front-footed, direct attacking football. His philosophy is all about disrupting the opposition press, winning the ball high up the pitch and scoring from artificial transitions (either due to turnovers or through line-breaking passes). <strong>Szoboszlai</strong> will be central to this and will surely build upon the excellent individual season he had last year.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-120-1024x768.png" alt="Szoboszlai FPL" class="wp-image-84983" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-120-1024x768.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-120-300x225.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-120-768x576.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-120-600x450.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-120.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>All Stats above are from FFHUB. For more Stats, Player Comparison, Points Prediction, Rate My Team AI Tool, AI Recommended Transfers, FPL Planners and much more to improve your FPL Game &#8211; <a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl" data-type="link" data-id="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Subscribe now for the 2026/27 season with an exclusive 50% </mark></a><a href="https://fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/?via=allaboutfpl"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">off discount</mark></a> and with a win your mini-league or money-back guarantee!</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>FACT: Szoboszlai will be playing the &#8216;Alex Scott&#8217; role at Liverpool this year. Scott returned 136 FPL points last season</strong> &#8211;<strong> 32 DEFCON points and a pretty good 0.21xGI/90.</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Hungarian midfielder is a popular FPL pick, currently sitting at around <strong>40% ownership</strong>, and his appeal comes from his <strong>ability to score points in several different ways</strong>. Last season, 32% of his points came from goals and assists, while a further 13% came from bonus points, 12.5% from DEFCON and 6% from clean sheets. The remaining points were largely appearance points, with Szoboszlai playing 90 minutes in all but one of his appearances and missing just two fixtures overall. This makes him one of the safest options in the bracket. Unlike many of his competitors, <strong>he offers both attacking potential and a reliable route to DEFCON and bonus points,</strong> while his excellent minutes record gives him a high floor.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Finally we have Arsenal&#8217;s <strong>Tzolis</strong>. The new, exciting forward signing for Arsenal looks set to start <strong>FPL GW1 against Coventry</strong> (home) after an electric performance against City in the community shield over the weekend. The Greek forward, who signed for Arsenal over the summer for £34m, put in a man of the match worthy performance in the pre-season cup competition. Over the course of the 90, <strong>Tzolis created 3 chances, 2 big chances and came away with 2 assists to his name</strong>. If he can do that against City, imagine what he could do to Coventry in FPL GW1&#8230;</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="740" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-18-at-13.33.59-740x1024.png" alt="Tzolis FPL" class="wp-image-84986" style="aspect-ratio:0.722998507201743;width:471px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-18-at-13.33.59-740x1024.png 740w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-18-at-13.33.59-217x300.png 217w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-18-at-13.33.59-768x1062.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-18-at-13.33.59-600x830.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-18-at-13.33.59.png 1044w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 740px) 100vw, 740px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">(<strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-27-pre-season-summary-of-all-20-premier-league-teams/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-27-pre-season-summary-of-all-20-premier-league-teams/"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Full Pre- Season Summary of all 20 Teams here</mark></a></strong>)</figcaption></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This stunning performance is a continuation of a great overall pre-season in which the <strong>Greek scored once and 6 times.</strong> Coming in at just 6.5m Tzolis is a fantastic, cheap way into a dangerous-looking Arsenal attack, which has been bolstered further by the midfield arrival of Bruno G. With Martinelli looking like he&#8217;s on the way out, Tzolis could be the long-term left-winger for Arsenal &#8211; even if they sign another option, at this point in the window it&#8217;s likely that Tzolis will start in the short term (GW1-GW4/5~).</p>



