<h3 class="wp-block-heading">FPL GW1 Scout Picks &#8211; Forwards</h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="172" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.37-1024x172.png" alt="FPL GW1 Scout Picks - Forwards" class="wp-image-84965" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.37-1024x172.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.37-300x50.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.37-768x129.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.37-1536x258.png 1536w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.37-600x101.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-16.15.37.png 1856w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Brobbey</strong> (6.0m), <strong>Haaland</strong> (15.5m) and <strong>Joao Pedro</strong> (7.5m) complete our FPL GW1 Scout Picks team&#8230;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Haaland</strong> starts for our FPL GW1 Scout Picks team in spite of his massive price hike to £15.5m&#8230; <strong>Considering his form at the world cup</strong>, his talent and his hunger to better last season&#8217;s somewhat dissapointing campaign, Haaland looks to be a good option to start the season. Furthermore, his ownership and haul potential makes him a dangerous option to not own &#8211; not falling behind in the early weeks of the FPL season is critical for those of us looking for high final Overalls&#8230; </p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-118.png" alt="Haaland FPL" class="wp-image-84981" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-118.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-118-300x225.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-118-768x576.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-118-600x450.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>All Stats above are from FFHUB. For more Stats, Player Comparison, Points Prediction, Rate My Team AI Tool, AI Recommended Transfers, FPL Planners and much more to improve your FPL Game &#8211; <a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl" data-type="link" data-id="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Subscribe now for the 2026/27 season with an exclusive 50% </mark></a><a href="https://fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/?via=allaboutfpl"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">off discount</mark></a> and with a win your mini-league or money-back guarantee!</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>FACT: Haaland&#8217;s xG/90 across his career in the Premier League is 0.95xG/90</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">While he did have a quiet game in the community shield and at times looked very isolated in the attack, there were a couple of moments where his personal talent shone through, and I have no doubt that he will easily score 20+ goals this season. <strong>Bournemouth have looked scary-good in pre-season</strong>, so I wouldn&#8217;t be doubling or tripling up on City assets going into GW1, but I do think that Haaland is a must-have to avoid early rank losses.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Another player who had an excellent world cup is Sunderland&#8217;s <strong>Brian Brobbey</strong>. For those managers looking to make an alliterative FPL team, Brobbey is a must-have along with Virgil Van Dijk, James Justin, Jeremy Jacquet, Van De Ven, Pedro Porro (I could go on)&#8230; Jokes aside, <strong>Brobbey scored 3 goals in 4 games at the world cup</strong>, and was a real handful for defenders. Last year in the league<strong> Brobbey scored 7 goals and assisted 1 across just under 2000 minutes of football</strong> &#8211; he looks set to start the season as the starting striker for the black cats and will be keen to better that record this time around.</p>


<img decoding="async" src="https://thumbs.smartframe.io/04742eb90cefa12a5e3ab9bae92c2b93/neimijGURKcI.webp?force-scraper=rss&#038;t=rss" alt="SmartFrame Image" />


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Sunderland face promoted Ipswich in the first game of the season</strong>, which has rendered a few of their players popular FPL options going into the season. Le Fee comes in at around 12% ownership, which is only marginally lower than Brobbey&#8217;s ~15% ownership (at time of writing) &#8211; both are good options for attacking <strong>Sunderland&#8217;s opening two fixtures of Ipswich and Fulham,</strong> though their games get significantly tougher after that point. Outside of Brobbey, DCL is another popular choice at this price point; I prefer Sunderland&#8217;s opening two fixtures, but DCL looks like the better long-term pick.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Finally we have <strong>Joao Pedro,</strong> who, unlike the other two strikers in this team, did not travel to the world cup in America. His lack of world cup involvement does mean, however, that <strong>JP has had a full pre-season under new manager Xabi Alonso</strong>, meaning he will not only be in a far better position in terms of recovery and rest, but also in terms of fitness and understanding of the new system. <strong>JP has scored <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-27-pre-season-summary-of-all-20-premier-league-teams/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-27-pre-season-summary-of-all-20-premier-league-teams/"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">7 goals and provided 2 assists across Chelsea&#8217;s 6 pre-season fixture</mark>s</a></strong> &#8211; he looks to be in majestic form going into the new campaign.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/how-chelsea-could-line-up-under-xabi-alonso-for-2026-27-season/"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="918" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-18-at-13.32.28-1024x918.png" alt="Chelsea FPL" class="wp-image-84985" style="width:482px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-18-at-13.32.28-1024x918.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-18-at-13.32.28-300x269.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-18-at-13.32.28-768x689.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-18-at-13.32.28-600x538.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-18-at-13.32.28.png 1202w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></a></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>FACT: JP&#8217;s 0.52xG/90 was the 7th highest in the league last season!</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Chelsea played a 3-4-3 in their most recent pre-season game, with <strong>Pedro, Rogers, Palmer as front 3 </strong>and Palestra and Neto as wingbacks. This is the front three that is likely to start GW1 against Fulham, though Welbeck, Estevao and others will surely be pushing fora starting spot too.<strong> Rogers looks to be an interesting option at 7.5m,</strong> but his lack of pre-season due to England&#8217;s involvement at the world cup and the competition for places in the team means that I would prioritise JP for the start of the season. It&#8217;s astonishing that JP&#8217;s price did not increase after a successful campaign last season in which the <strong>Brazilian scored 15 and provided 5 assists for Chelsea.</strong></p>



