		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://allaboutfpl.com/?p=84953</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>In this post, we take a look at the Best FPL Budget Midfielders. We take into account individual/team form as well as fixtures and stats.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-budget-fpl-midfielders-for-26-27-season-4-5m-to-6-0m/">Best Budget FPL Midfielders for 26/27 Season | £4.5m to £6.0m</a> appeared first on <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com">ALLABOUTFPL: Your one stop place for all FPL tips, FPL captain picks, FPL news, FPL players, previews, reviews,differential picks, analysis and weekly updates.</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This is the final article in my <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/category/fpl-midfielders/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">midfield series</mark></a></strong>, where we move into the budget options priced between £4.5m and £6.0m.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There are some more well-known names in the £6.0m bracket, but hopefully I can also highlight a few hidden gems along the way. It is quite a big pool of players, and my gut feeling is that it could take a few Gameweeks before we really understand who the best options are in this bracket.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">What I want to do with this article is give managers a bit of an insight into the players I am leaning towards ahead of Gameweek 1. Some are safer bets, while others are more of a risk.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For me personally, when I am looking at this price bracket, I am primarily looking for someone who is nailed on for minutes. If they can also offer some DEFCON points or goal involvements, even better. There are even a couple of penalty takers in here, which could make them particularly attractive options.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Realistically, this is the sort of player I am probably going to have sitting on my bench or occupying that 4th midfielder role, as I am likely to start the season with a 3-4-3. So for me, the priority is nailed-on minutes, and if we can pick up some DEFCON points or the odd goal or assist along the way, that is a bonus.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Check out the other parts of the <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/category/fpl-midfielders/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">FPL Midfielders series</mark></a></strong>:</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-premium-fpl-midfielders-8-0-12-0-million-26-27-season/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Best Premium FPL Midfielders (£8.0 – £12.0 Million)</mark></strong></a><br><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-mid-price-fpl-midfielders-for-the-26-27-season-6-5-to-7-5m/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Best Mid-Price FPL Midfielders £6.5 to 7.5M</mark></strong></a></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Written by <a href="https://www.instagram.com/bazzabarrett20/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Jack Barrett</mark></strong></a>, do follow him on <a href="https://www.instagram.com/bazzabarrett20/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Instagram</mark></strong></a>!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/category/ultimate-2026-27-fpl-pre-season-guide/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/category/ultimate-2026-27-fpl-pre-season-guide/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color"><strong>Link to all our 2026/27 Pre-Season articles</strong></mark></a> including all team pre-season friendly updates, best drafts, fixture analysis, position-wise analysis, differentials, players to target, budget enablers and more. Completely free to access as well!</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center"><strong>Budget FPL Midfielder</strong>s</h2>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Iliman Ndiaye £6.0m</h3>


<img decoding="async" src="https://thumbs.smartframe.io/1970e2615a4bf4d8c7ab2416a1cc8d79/evfceZnsQOUa.webp?force-scraper=rss&#038;t=rss" alt="SmartFrame Image" />


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The first player I want to look at in this article is Everton&#8217;s Iliman Ndiaye.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ndiaye is likely to be Everton&#8217;s first-choice penalty taker, having already scored<strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-27-pre-season-summary-of-all-20-premier-league-teams/" data-type="post" data-id="84802" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"> <mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">2 from 2 penalties in pre-season</mark></a></strong>, and that immediately makes him an interesting option at £6.0m.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He scored <strong>6 goals and provided 3 assists last season, racking up 128 points</strong>, and he is currently the most selected midfielder in this price bracket, with nearly 16% ownership. His opening fixtures are also really appealing, with Everton facing Crystal Palace, Bournemouth, Manchester United, Tottenham, Ipswich and Hull in their first 6 Gameweeks. That gives him a really nice run of fixtures to start the season, including 2 of his opening 2 games against teams with new managers.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For me, the biggest attraction is that Ndiaye looks very likely to be nailed on for Everton. There was some talk of him leaving earlier in the transfer window, but he has stayed put for now, and if he remains first choice on penalties, I think that makes him one of the stronger options in this price bracket.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He might not be the player that immediately jumps off the page when you look at the midfield options, but when you combine his expected minutes, penalty duties and opening fixtures, I think Ndiaye is a really appealing option at just £6.0m.</p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Fantasy Football Hub(FFHUB) Free AI Team Rating Tool</mark></a></strong></p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1000" height="596" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84095" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596.png 1000w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596-300x179.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596-768x458.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596-600x358.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px" /></a><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Get your team rated by <strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" data-type="link" data-id="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Fantasy Football Hub</mark></a></strong>&#8216;s AI Team Rating tool for free (Click on the image above to get your team rated).</figcaption></figure>
</div>


<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Kevin Schade £6.0m</h3>


<img decoding="async" src="https://thumbs.smartframe.io/598d587f82f0613dc60f89d2daf94a61/brfcUknGAioO.webp?force-scraper=rss&#038;t=rss" alt="SmartFrame Image" />


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The next player I want to look at is Brentford&#8217;s Kevin Schade, and this is probably one of the more exciting options in this price bracket.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">No midfielder managed more big chances than Schade in the Premier League last season. He scored <strong>8 goals and provided 5 assists, giving him 125 points across the campaign.</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">What is particularly interesting is that his underlying numbers were even better than his actual output. In simple terms, his expected goal involvements were significantly higher than the 13 goal involvements he actually produced, which suggests there could be plenty more to come.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="986" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-10.21.26-PM-986x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84973" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-10.21.26-PM-986x1024.png 986w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-10.21.26-PM-289x300.png 289w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-10.21.26-PM-768x798.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-10.21.26-PM-600x623.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-17-at-10.21.26-PM.png 1178w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 986px) 100vw, 986px" /></a></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At the time of writing, <strong>Schade is selected by just 2.7% of managers</strong>, so he is a very interesting differential. He opens the season against Tottenham before facing Leeds, Sunderland and Bournemouth, giving him some decent fixtures to start the campaign.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The downside, however, is his minutes. Schade started 32 games last season, but only completed the full 90 minutes in 18 of those matches. He was regularly substituted before the final whistle, so while I really like his attacking potential, there is a slight concern over how much time he will actually spend on the pitch.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He also faces new competition this season from Jaidon Anthony, who Brentford signed from Burnley, so that is another situation worth monitoring. Schade has already scored <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-27-pre-season-summary-of-all-20-premier-league-teams/" data-type="post" data-id="84802" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">2 goals and provided 2 assists in pre-season</mark></a></strong>, so he will be hoping to hit the ground running and support Igor Thiago, who is expected to lead the line once again.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For me, <strong>Schade is probably the most dangerous attacking option in this bracket</strong>, but the minutes are the concern. As I said at the start, my priority is nailed on minutes, so that is something I will definitely be keeping an eye on before Gameweek 1.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel=" noreferrer noopener"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/top-10-big-chances-gw1-38-1-1024x768.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84954" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/top-10-big-chances-gw1-38-1-1024x768.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/top-10-big-chances-gw1-38-1-300x225.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/top-10-big-chances-gw1-38-1-768x576.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/top-10-big-chances-gw1-38-1-600x450.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/top-10-big-chances-gw1-38-1.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></a><figcaption class="wp-element-caption"><strong>Data from FFHUB.</strong> For more Stats, Player Comparison, Points Prediction, Rate My Team AI Tool, AI-recommended transfers, FPL Planners and much more to improve your FPL Game &#8211; <strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl" data-type="link" data-id="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Subscribe now for the 2026/27 season with an exclusive 50% </mark></a><a href="https://fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/?via=allaboutfpl"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">off discount</mark></a> </strong>and with a win your mini-league or money-back guarantee!</figcaption></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read:</strong> <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-2027-fpl-team-structure-guide-with-drafts-ratings/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-2027-fpl-team-structure-guide-with-drafts-ratings/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">FPL Team Structure Guide with Drafts, AI Team Rating, Formations, Pros, Cons and Key Notes</mark></a></strong></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Enzo Le Fée £6.0m</h3>


<img decoding="async" src="https://thumbs.smartframe.io/c78749ece7fd074ea5dc1889e7c53f0f/esmelzkt4qiC.webp?force-scraper=rss&#038;t=rss" alt="SmartFrame Image" />


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The next player I want to look at is a very eye-catching name, and one that I was quite intrigued by when I saw his price. I thought Enzo Le Fée might come in at around £6.5m, so £6.0m immediately felt very reasonable to me.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Le Fée accumulated 147 points last season, scoring 5 goals and providing 6 assists. Only James Garner scored more points last season among the players in this price bracket, although Garner is unfortunately injured and looks set to miss the start of the season. This means Le Fée is last season&#8217;s highest-scoring midfielder who is fit and available in this price bracket. He was also joint-top for assists at Sunderland and averaged 4.1 points per match. Additionally, he picked up 12 points from DEFCON last season, averaging 9.66 defensive contributions per start, so there is a nice additional source of points there.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">What makes him even more appealing is his set-piece involvement. In Sunderland&#8217;s most recent pre-season friendly, Diarra was benched, which should make Le Fée the first-choice penalty taker heading into the new season. He should also continue to be involved with corners and free kicks. Le Fée has already scored 3 goals in pre-season, while Sunderland have a really appealing opening run of Ipswich, Fulham and Brentford.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Just to put into perspective how impressive his debut season for Sunderland was, Le Fée scored more FPL points than the likes of Matheus Cunha, Rayan Cherki, Florian Wirtz and Cole Palmer last season. Those are all big names who sit in the premium price brackets, so I think that is worth highlighting.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For me, Le Fée is a really attractive option at £6.0m. He looks nailed on for minutes, has attacking potential, DEFCON potential and looks set to have penalty duties as well.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you haven&#8217;t quite got the money for Le Fée, I would also keep an eye on his teammate and captain, Granit Xhaka, who comes in at £5.5m. Xhaka was a player I owned a lot last season and he did exactly the job I want from this sort of player. He can sit on my bench and come into the starting XI when needed. He scored 124 points last season, with 1 goal and 6 assists, but most importantly he picked up 26 points from DEFCON.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For me, I think I can justify spending the extra £0.5m on Le Fée because of the potential penalty duties, but Xhaka is certainly one to keep an eye on.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/e-le-f-e-vs-xhaka-1024x768.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84955" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/e-le-f-e-vs-xhaka-1024x768.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/e-le-f-e-vs-xhaka-300x225.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/e-le-f-e-vs-xhaka-768x576.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/e-le-f-e-vs-xhaka-600x450.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/e-le-f-e-vs-xhaka.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></a><figcaption class="wp-element-caption"><strong>Data from FFHUB.</strong> For more Stats, Player Comparison, Points Prediction, Rate My Team AI Tool, AI-recommended transfers, FPL Planners and much more to improve your FPL Game &#8211; <strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl" data-type="link" data-id="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Subscribe now for the 2026/27 season with an exclusive 50% </mark></a><a href="https://fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/?via=allaboutfpl"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">off discount</mark></a> </strong>and with a win your mini-league or money-back guarantee!</figcaption></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read: </strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-27-pl-season-predicted-gw1-lineups-of-all-20-pl-teams/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">2026/27 PL Season: Predicted GW1 Lineups of All 20 PL Teams</mark></strong></a></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Pascal Groß £5.5m</h3>


<img decoding="async" src="https://thumbs.smartframe.io/1ffbae35d432d0d71911ca2a0b209fbb/prsiVlLiVj4t.webp?force-scraper=rss&#038;t=rss" alt="SmartFrame Image" />


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The next player I want to look at is one of the more experienced options in this price bracket, Brighton&#8217;s Pascal Groß.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I really like Groß at £5.5m, particularly because he looks set to be nailed on for minutes. He is something of a club legend at Brighton, so much so that the Seagulls brought him back to the club in January, and he played 85 minutes or more in 18 of the 19 appearances he made after returning.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He has already started to show some promising signs in pre-season too, with 1 goal and 1 assist, while last season he scored 1 goal and provided 6 assists in just 18 starts. He is currently selected by around 11.5% of managers and averaged 4.1 points per match.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">One of the biggest attractions for me is the set-piece potential. With Danny Welbeck moving to Chelsea, I can see Groß taking on penalty duties, while he should also continue to be involved with free kicks and corners from both sides.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Interestingly, only Ryan Cherki and Bruno Fernandes recorded more assists per appearance than Groß last season. Something I think managers need to bear in mind when looking at his numbers from last season. If you simply look at his overall points, goals and assists, you might think there are better options elsewhere. However, it is important to remember that Groß only made 18 starts because he rejoined Brighton in January. He wasn&#8217;t being left out of the team, he simply wasn&#8217;t at the club for the first half of the season. The fact that he still managed 6 assists in those 18 starts is therefore really encouraging and gives us a good indication of what he could offer over a full season.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For me, the only real concern is his age. Groß is now 35, and there will understandably be some questions over whether he can remain a regular starter throughout the season, particularly with Brighton also competing in European football. That is the one thing that would make me slightly nervous about selecting him.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">However, I do think he looks nailed on to start the season in the Premier League, and if he can continue to get regular minutes, his set-piece involvement makes him a very appealing option at £5.5m.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I also don&#8217;t think I can quite justify spending the extra £0.5m on Jack Hinshelwood at the moment. Hinshelwood may offer a little more from open play, but Groß has the added attraction of penalties and set pieces, which is exactly the sort of thing I am looking for in this price bracket. For a player who is likely to sit in my 4/5th midfielder spot, I think Groß could be a really smart pick.</p>


