<h2 class="wp-block-heading">So which Budget FPL Midfielders should managers pick?</h2>


<img decoding="async" src="https://thumbs.smartframe.io/04742eb90cefa12a5e3ab9bae92c2b93/neimfZ1BrTrJ.webp?force-scraper=rss&#038;t=rss" alt="SmartFrame Image" />


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">So overall, those are the players that I feel are the best options in this price bracket.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If I&#8217;m being completely honest, my final thoughts are that Enzo Le Fée is my preferred £6.0m option, with Iliman Ndiaye a very close second. I think both are really good options, but I&#8217;m just leaning slightly more towards Le Fée at the moment, mainly because of the combination of his attacking potential, DEFCON, set pieces and what looks like penalty duties.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">When it comes to the £5.5m options, Pascal Groß is probably my favourite. His experience, set-piece involvement and the fact that he looks likely to be on penalties make him really appealing for me, particularly when I&#8217;m looking for someone to fill that 4/5th midfielder role.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you want to take a bit more of a punt, then Mamadou Sangaré is the one I&#8217;d be looking at. I don&#8217;t expect him to be producing the big hauls that you might get from some of the premium midfielders, but if he can establish himself as a regular starter, his DEFCON numbers could make him a really useful FPL asset. Given the amount Brentford have invested in him, you&#8217;d expect him to be given a real opportunity to establish himself in the team, and at £5.5m, I think he could prove to be a bit of a steal.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">One other thing I would say is that I would definitely prioritise finding that extra £0.5m to move up to a £5.5m midfielder rather than settling for a £5.0m option. Purely based on what we know heading into Gameweek 1, I don&#8217;t think there is a particularly reliable option below £5.5m at the moment. Diego Gómez could potentially change that if he proves his fitness, but otherwise, I think you can justify spending the extra £0.5m on the likes of Groß, Sangaré or even Xhaka. For me, that extra £0.5m could make a big difference when it comes to having someone you actually trust to step into your starting XI when needed.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">So, if it was my squad right now, I&#8217;d probably be going for Le Fée and Groß, but I would have absolutely no problem with managers taking a chance on Ndiaye or Sangaré instead. In a price bracket like this, there isn&#8217;t necessarily one correct answer, and I think we could see a few of these players emerge as very good options once the season gets underway.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Finally, I just want to wish all managers the very best of luck for the start of the season. I&#8217;m sure there will be plenty of changes to our drafts between now and Friday evening, and that&#8217;s completely fine. There is no right or wrong player that you should be selecting for your team. It&#8217;s all personal preference, so play around with your drafts, have some fun with it and go with the players you feel most comfortable with.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Thank you very much for reading, and I wish you all the best of luck for the new season. Hopefully there are plenty of green arrows coming our way over the next few weeks!</p>



