			</item>
		<item>
		<title>FPL GW1 Bench Boost Drafts -BB1 vs BB2 vs Later &#124; 26/27 Season</title>
		<link>https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/fpl-gw1-bench-boost-drafts-bb1-vs-bb2-vs-later-26-27-season/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Rohan Bajaj]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 11:14:52 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[FPL Bench Boost]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[FPL GW1]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[FPL GW1 Ultimate Guide and Tips]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Game week Preview]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Ultimate 2026/27 FPL Pre-Season Guide]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[bb1 vs bb2]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[best gw1 bench boost draft]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[best gw1 drafts for 2026/27 season]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[fantasy premier league bench boost]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[fpl bench boost]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[fpl chip strategy]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[gameweek 1 bnech boost]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[gw1 bench boost]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[gw1 bench boost vs gw2 bench boost]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[gw1 best team]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[GW1 draft]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[gw2 bench boost]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[when to play bench boost in fpl]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://allaboutfpl.com/?p=84801</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>In this article, We take a look at the Best FPL GW1 Bench Boost Drafts compare with GW2 Bench Boost as well. </p>
<p>The post <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/fpl-gw1-bench-boost-drafts-bb1-vs-bb2-vs-later-26-27-season/">FPL GW1 Bench Boost Drafts -BB1 vs BB2 vs Later | 26/27 Season</a> appeared first on <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com">ALLABOUTFPL: Your one stop place for all FPL tips, FPL captain picks, FPL news, FPL players, previews, reviews,differential picks, analysis and weekly updates.</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Hello and welcome to another 2026/27 FPL season blog! With GW1&#8217;s deadline just a week away (Friday 21 August at 18:30 BST), the biggest debate right now seems to be about the Bench Boost (BB) chip. It&#8217;s another season with two full sets of chips to use, one before and one after GW19. This essentially means FPL managers can&#8217;t just save their BB chip for a double GW, forcing most to use it in a single GW instead.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There&#8217;s a genuine divide on the efficacy of the chip and the thought process around it. One faction wants to get rid of it early and focus on the playing XI going forward, while the other prefers to plan for it with more data in hand. In this article, we&#8217;ll look at FPL drafts built around three broad strategies: GW1 BB, GW2 BB, and a BB Later draft. Let&#8217;s break down the case for each.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/category/ultimate-2026-27-fpl-pre-season-guide/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/category/ultimate-2026-27-fpl-pre-season-guide/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color"><strong>Link to all our 2026/27 Pre-Season articles</strong></mark></a> including all team pre-season friendly updates, best drafts, fixture analysis, position-wise analysis, differentials, players to target, budget enablers and more. Completely free to access as well!</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center">FPL GW1 Bench Boost Draft | 2026/27 season</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The GW1 BB draft bets heavily on pre-season knowledge and spillover from last season&#8217;s data. It follows the basic assumptions that promoted teams will be leaky at the back, and that last season&#8217;s league leaders will continue to dominate these games.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">The Value-Bench (2-premium)</h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="872" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-99-1024x872.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84865" style="width:608px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-99-1024x872.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-99-300x255.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-99-768x654.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-99-600x511.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-99.png 1250w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption"><strong>FPL GW1 BB Draft | Value-bench approach</strong></figcaption></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This Draft also has a<strong> <a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" data-type="link" data-id="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">92% AI Team Rating</mark></a></strong> and <strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" data-type="link" data-id="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">73 Predicted Points</mark></a></strong> for GW1 Bench Boost according to Fantasy Football Hub. <strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" data-type="link" data-id="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Get your FPL Teams rated for FREE in seconds. </mark></a></strong></p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="813" height="877" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-110.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84937" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-110.png 813w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-110-278x300.png 278w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-110-768x828.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-110-600x647.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 813px) 100vw, 813px" /></figure>
</div>


<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Fantasy Football Hub(FFHUB) Free AI Team Rating Tool</mark></a></strong></p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1000" height="596" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84095" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596.png 1000w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596-300x179.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596-768x458.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596-600x358.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px" /></a><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Get your team rated by <strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" data-type="link" data-id="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Fantasy Football Hub</mark></a></strong>&#8216;s AI Team Rating tool for free (Click on the image above to get your team rated).</figcaption></figure>
</div>


<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Under this draft, the idea is to go with a standard two-premium squad, with a bench just good enough to make Bench Boost worthwhile. Key Bench Boost targets:</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Target Sunderland away at Ipswich: <strong>Hume at 4.5m</strong> is a useful rotation option alongside your other defenders, despite returning to his right-back duties rather than staying forward as an &#8220;OOP&#8221; option.<strong> Enzo Le Fée (6.0m)</strong> demands a small premium but is confirmed on penalties for SUN (alongside Diarra) and he was good for <strong>147 points</strong> and a <strong>24.2% DEFCON hit rate</strong> last season. Sunderland&#8217;s fixture run also helps the bench beyond GW1, into the next five weeks. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Pascal Groß at 5.5m</strong> is one of the best budget midfield options. He&#8217;s secure for minutes and could be on penalties, and he still returned <strong>78 points</strong> from just <strong>18 starts</strong> last season. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Caicedo at the same price is a close consideration too, with a stronger DEFCON focus, he hit the DEFCON threshold in <strong>40.6%</strong> of his games last season. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>O&#8217;Shea at 4.0m</strong> becomes bench fodder in the long run, once he&#8217;s served his purpose for Bench Boost. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Kinsky</strong> and <strong>Verbruggen</strong> combo at 9.0m is a cheap entry into two playing GKs, Verbruggen alone had managed <strong>130 points</strong> last season.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The rest of the team largely picks itself, with minimal sacrifices elsewhere. Haaland, Bruno, and Mbeumo offer plenty of structural strength, Mbeumo could start up-front for United. João Pedro, Szoboszlai, and DCL round out the rest, with DCL having returned <strong>142 points</strong> and <strong>14 goals</strong> last season. Overall, this team offers a strong balance between BB GW1 and premium firepower up top.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read: </strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-27-pre-season-summary-of-all-20-premier-league-teams/"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">2026/27 Pre-Season Summary of All 20 Premier League Teams</mark></strong></a></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"> Stronger Bench (1-premium)</h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="872" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-98-1024x872.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84864" style="width:587px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-98-1024x872.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-98-300x255.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-98-768x654.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-98-600x511.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-98.png 1250w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">FPL GW1 BB Draft | Strong-bench approach</figcaption></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Swapping out Haaland for the opening weeks allows for a stronger overall squad. This frees up enough budget for a bench of <strong>Brobbey, Ballard </strong>(away at Ipswich), and <strong>Kadioğlu</strong> or another 4.5m defender. Going forward, Brobbey can be a strong bench option to step in when needed, having returned <strong>92 points</strong> from just <strong>22 starts</strong> last season. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A strong five-man midfield of <strong>Semenyo</strong>, <strong>Mbeumo</strong>, <strong>Szoboszlai</strong>, and <strong>Rice</strong> gives a good mix of attacking threat and DEFCON potential, Rice&#8217;s <strong>40% DEFCON hit rate</strong> last season ranks right up there with the best in the league. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Another option in this draft is you can downgrade Rice to Tzolis who has had a fantastic pre-season with 1 Goal and 6 Assists. You can use those funds to upgrade Thiago to Isak. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This Draft also has a<strong> </strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" data-type="link" data-id="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">92% AI Team Rating </mark></strong></a>and <strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" data-type="link" data-id="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">72 Predicted Points</mark></a></strong> for GW1 Bench Boost according to Fantasy Football Hub. <strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" data-type="link" data-id="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Get your FPL Teams rated for FREE in seconds</mark></a>.</strong> </p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="823" height="868" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-111.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84939" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-111.png 823w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-111-284x300.png 284w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-111-768x810.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-111-600x633.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 823px) 100vw, 823px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This also allows for quick swaps to in-form midfielders as early-season trends emerge.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read: </strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/premier-league-penalty-set-piece-takers-2026-27-pl-season/"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Premier League Penalty &amp; Set Piece Takers | 2026/27 PL Season</mark></strong></a></p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">FPL GW2 Bench Boost Draft | 2026/27 Season</h2>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="804" height="823" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-112.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84942" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-112.png 804w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-112-293x300.png 293w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-112-768x786.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-112-600x614.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 804px) 100vw, 804px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This Draft also has a<strong> <a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" data-type="link" data-id="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">85% AI Team Rating and 56 Predicted Points</mark></a></strong> for GW1 according to Fantasy Football Hub.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The most appealing factor about GW2 BB is that it allows managers to be aggressive, you can go ultra-cheap on the bench thanks to the Coventry-Hull fixture.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A triple-up with <strong>Van Ewijk (4.0m) </strong>and <strong>Thomas</strong> <strong>(4.0m) </strong>in defence, plus <strong>Simms (5.0m)</strong> further forward. Placing all your bets on Coventry naturally carries its own risk, but the upside is not spending excess money on the bench, and potentially saving the Wildcard for a later date. Simms(5.0) is mentioned in this draft and there is 0.5 million left in the bank. Awoniyi(5.5) is linked heavily and close to a move to Coventry which could mean that he could take his place. Have a  close eye on that news before the GW1 deadline. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read: </strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/fpl-rotational-pairs-combinations-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">FPL Rotational Pairs &amp; Combinations for the 2026/27 FPL Season</mark></strong></a></p>



<h4 class="wp-block-heading">GW2 Bench Boost Projection:</h4>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="841" height="852" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-114.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84945" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-114.png 841w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-114-296x300.png 296w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-114-768x778.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-114-600x608.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 841px) 100vw, 841px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This Draft also has a<strong> <a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" data-type="link" data-id="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">88% AI Team Rating and 67 Predicted Points</mark></a></strong> for GW2 Bench Boost according to <strong>Fantasy Football Hub</strong>. <strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" data-type="link" data-id="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Get your FPL Teams rated for FREE in seconds</mark></a>.</strong> </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Petrovic</strong>, at home to Everton, swaps in for Verbruggen to improve the bench. Chelsea at home to Brighton allows a <strong>João Pedro </strong>and <strong>Caicedo</strong> double-up. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Wirtz</strong> and <strong>Schade</strong> offer two differential punts in midfield, Schade racked up <strong>125 points</strong> last season on pure attacking output. <strong>Ballard</strong> offers decent goal threat and DEFCON potential (a <strong>58.3% hit rate</strong> last season) for a three-man defensive line to start the season with.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A one-premium version of this draft looks similar, swapping out Haaland or Fernandes and distributing the money among semi-premiums like Semenyo, Thiago, and Gabriel.</p>



