<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center">Other FPL Bench Boost Windows</h2>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">GW4 WC to GW5 BB Strategy</h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="626" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-106-626x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84908" style="width:453px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-106-626x1024.png 626w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-106-184x300.png 184w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-106-600x981.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-106.png 734w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 626px) 100vw, 626px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">FPL GW5 Fixtures 2026/27 Season</figcaption></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">GW4 lines up with an early fixture swing, and also leaves enough information to weed out the pre-season hype picks and risky-minutes players. This leads into a GW5 Bench Boost, wrapping both chips up before the three-week international break.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Fixtures to target:</strong> <strong>Everton</strong> (Tarkowski, whose <strong>59.5% DEFCON hit rate</strong> led all defenders last season, and Ndiaye) hosting Ipswich; <strong>Man City</strong> options that might emerge hosting Sunderland; <strong>Nott&#8217;m Forest</strong> (N. Williams, MGW, and potentially Igor Jesus) at home to Coventry; and <strong>Newcastle</strong> (Wissa, Thiaw, and others) against Hull.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">These fixtures offer a good mix of cheap player options to build a bench around. Managers could also use the Wildcard to move away from a Man United-heavy line-up by this point, if that&#8217;s the direction they went in GW1.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read: </strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/top-mid-priced-premium-fpl-forwards6-0-for-2026-27-season/"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Top Mid Priced &amp; Premium FPL Forwards(>6.0) for 2026/27 season</mark></strong></a></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">GW6 WC to GW7-9 BB Window</h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="545" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-105-1024x545.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84907" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-105-1024x545.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-105-300x160.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-105-768x409.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-105-1536x818.png 1536w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-105-2048x1090.png 2048w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-105-600x319.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption"><strong>FPL 2026/27 Season Fixtures</strong></figcaption></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The GW6 WC pairing is the more patient version, landing right after the 3-week international break. That patience naturally rewards you with plenty of information to plan the BB chip. It can be fitted somewhere between GW7 and GW9 based on WC plans.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>GW7 Fixture Targets:</strong> Fulham, Man United, Man City, and Spurs become the key sides to target to optimise the Bench Boost.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>GW8 Fixture Targets:</strong> Fulham, Brentford, and Nott&#8217;m Forest players can all appear on the bench. Sunderland vs Leeds could be a nail-biter, with options from both sides in DCL, Brobbey, Le Fée, and the Sunderland defence.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>GW9 Fixture Targets:</strong> This echoes the GW2 Bench Boost strategy, only this time it&#8217;s Hull and Ipswich meeting each other, with O&#8217;Shea and Diop as the options (worth monitoring his fitness). Sunderland and Coventry make up the second fixture to watch, with plenty of cheap options from both sides.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Pros</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>More information to identify teams and players to target. </li>



<li>Potentially selling Bruno after his early fixtures against Ipswich and Hull, which naturally allows you to redistribute money across the team over two or three free transfers (saving the WC for after BB). </li>



<li>Allows you to optimise the playing XI in the opening weeks and focus transfers on in-form players. </li>



<li>WC could pair naturally with BB opportunities (the combinations discussed above).</li>



<li>An improved team-value allowing for a pricier bench.</li>
</ul>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Cons</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>A WC-into-BB strategy can end up being short-sighted if it focuses too heavily on the bench. This can leave a lot of money tied up on the bench until the second WC becomes available.</li>



<li>The counter-argument to improved team-value is missing out on those same cheap options as they undergo price rises.</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read: <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-27-fpl-chip-strategy-guide-first-half-of-the-season/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-27-fpl-chip-strategy-guide-first-half-of-the-season/"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Ultimate Chip Strategy Guide for 2026/27 Season</mark></a></strong></p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Conclusion</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Your <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-27-fpl-chip-strategy-guide-first-half-of-the-season/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-27-fpl-chip-strategy-guide-first-half-of-the-season/"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Chip strategy </mark></a></strong>ultimately depends on your relationship with the BB chip and how it has treated you in the past. Managers who play it before the WC want to get it out of the way and focus on the XI afterwards. For many others, though, a post-WC BB presents more points-scoring potential to grab. What matters most is decent planning so the chip doesn&#8217;t eat too much out of your free transfers and pressing the button in panic. There will of course be exceptions, but sticking to a plan makes life a lot easier, especially with Triple Captain and Free Hit still to be explored.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Thank you for reading this blog and see you in the next one!</p>



