<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Alexander Isak – 9.0 Forward &#8211; Liverpool</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-27-1024x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84920" style="width:648px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-27-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-27-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-27-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-27-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-27-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-27.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Pros :</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>When he is injury-free and not distracted with transfer rumors, Isak is a hell of a player. The proof is in the pudding, as he scored 23 and 21 Goals in the 2 full seasons he played at Newcastle. He even had 10 Assists across those 2 seasons. He even has penalties now in his corner with Mo Salah departing Liverpool.</li>



<li>Liverpool have the best 5 fixtures to start the season as they face a Newcastle team in transition and then face teams like Forest, Fulham at home, and promoted Ipswich and Bournemouth away. Iraola is a front-foot manager, unlike Slot, and transformed Bournemouth’s attack completely. Expect him to have the same effect on Liverpool. With Ekitike out injured, Isak is now expected to play most of the minutes, and he does seem to be getting back to his best, as evidenced by his displays in the World Cup in the summer. If he can stay fit, expect him to have another 20+ Goal season.</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Isak in pre-season: 100+ Minutes, <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/26bd.png" alt="⚽" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f170.png" alt="🅰" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /></strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Cons :</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>His injury record is the only concern at the moment. If he can stay fit, Isak looks to be a brilliant option in FPL this season.</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read:</strong> <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/premier-league-penalty-set-piece-takers-2026-27-pl-season/"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Premier League Penalty &amp; Set Piece Takers | 2026/27 PL Season</mark></strong></a></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Ollie Watkins – 8.0 Forward &#8211; Aston Villa</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-29-1024x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84925" style="width:670px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-29-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-29-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-29-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-29-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-29-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-29.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Pros :</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Consistent Ollie Watkins. 15, 19, 16 and 16 Goals in the last 4 Premier League seasons. 167 FPL Points is the lowest he has scored in the last 4 FPL seasons. That is remarkable consistency. Watkins ranked 3<sup>rd</sup> among Forwards for Big Chances (24) and 4<sup>th</sup> for xG (15.14) last season.</li>
</ul>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/watkins-landscape-1-1-1024x768.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84923" style="width:752px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/watkins-landscape-1-1-1024x768.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/watkins-landscape-1-1-300x225.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/watkins-landscape-1-1-768x576.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/watkins-landscape-1-1-600x450.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/watkins-landscape-1-1.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Villa are also one of the few teams that have the same coach as last season, and that itself is a positive, as most Premier League teams will need time to adjust to the new tactics of their new coaches. From Gameweek 3, Villa’s fixtures ease up, and I expect Watkins to be the focal point of the Villa attack again this season.</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Cons :</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>The departures of Rogers could hurt Villa’s creativity, plus 2 tough games to begin the season makes Watkins an avoid in the 1<sup>st</sup> 2 Games of the season.</li>



<li>Watkins has also been linked to a move away from Villa, and although that is unlikely to happen, best to jump on him after the transfer window closes after Gameweek 2. Gameweek 3 against Hull City seems to be the perfect window.</li>
</ul>



