<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>The Gunners (Viktor Gyokeres and Kai Havertz) – 7.5 Forwards &#8211; Arsenal</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-26-1024x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84918" style="width:670px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-26-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-26-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-26-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-26-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-26-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-26.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Pros :</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Gyokeres scored 14 Goals in only 26 Starts last season and this was the 5<sup>th</sup> best among Forwards. Having penalties in his locker helps and also surrounded by quality players such as Saka, Odegaard, Eze and Rice will get the best out of any striker. Gyokeres is also usually preferred to start against the lower ranked teams in the League</li>



<li>Havertz is often favored by Arteta in the tougher games and that was in full evidence when Havertz started the Champions League final and also scored. Although Havertz only started 7 Games last season, he still scored 2 Goals in the League and even got 3 Assists (more than Gyokeres managed). Havertz’s all round play is appreciated by every manager and he should feature more regularly this season after his injury fears are now behind him.</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Havertz in pre-season: <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/26bd.png" alt="⚽" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /><strong><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/26bd.png" alt="⚽" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /></strong></strong>, 250+ minutes</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Gyokeres in pre-season: <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/26bd.png" alt="⚽" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /></strong>, 200+ minutes</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Cons :</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Gyokeres will need to improve his overall game to become Arsenal’s main man. Otherwise, Arteta may start playing Havertz more and more as he contributes a much more balanced approach to the team.</li>



<li>Injury concerns are Havertz’s main issue. One more problem is that with Bruno Guimarães signing for Arsenal, Havertz’s role in midfield now seems much more limited. He will mostly be played as the Striker and usually in the tougher games, where goal-scoring opportunities are likely to be much less.</li>
</ul>



