<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Joao Pedro – 7.5 Forward &#8211; Chelsea</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-12-1-1024x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84361" style="width:682px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-12-1-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-12-1-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-12-1-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-12-1-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-12-1-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-12-1.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Pros :</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>He is currently the 2<sup>nd</sup> most owned player in the game, before the season has kicked off and for good reason. He has had a summer off from the World Cup and is fully rested and ready to prove a point to the Brazil National Team. He scored 15 Goals and got 9 Assists last season and got 177 FPL points, which was the 4<sup>th</sup> best among Forwards. He is also on fire in pre-season, having scored 7 Goals in 5 games so far.</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Joao Pedro in pre-season: 300+ Minutes, <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/26bd.png" alt="⚽" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/26bd.png" alt="⚽" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/26bd.png" alt="⚽" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/26bd.png" alt="⚽" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/26bd.png" alt="⚽" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/26bd.png" alt="⚽" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/26bd.png" alt="⚽" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f170.png" alt="🅰" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f170.png" alt="🅰" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /></strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>One of Pedro’s main advantages over other forwards is his all-round game. He created 29 chances and 6 Big Chances last season and got the most number of assists among Forwards. Usually playing as a Forward, he can also play just behind the striker. That versatility comes in handy during injuries to other players.</li>



<li>With an attacking coach like Xavi Alonso and players like Palmer and Rogers feeding him chances, he should get even more opportunities this season. Lack of European commitments will also help Chelsea to fully focus on the League this season.</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Cons :</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Not much at the moment, but Chelsea’s bloated squad could lead to some rotation during the hectic Christmas period.</li>
</ul>



