<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Benjamin Sesko – 7.0 Forward &#8211; Manchester United</strong></h3>


<img decoding="async" src="https://thumbs.smartframe.io/04742eb90cefa12a5e3ab9bae92c2b93/neimh1rpv4uM.webp?force-scraper=rss&#038;t=rss" alt="SmartFrame Image" />


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Pros :</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Sesko ended the season strongly with 11 Goals and 2 Assists from 17 starts after initially struggling at the beginning of the season. He did much better under Carrick than under Amorim, often coming off the bench to grab winners for United. He is United’s Main Striker and will likely improve under Carrick’s guidance this season.</li>



<li>Getting chances will never be a problem with United’s rich source of chance creators like Bruno, Cunha and Mbeumo.</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Cons :</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Currently, he is not expected to start the 1st few weeks as his pre-season was disrupted by a shin injury. He will miss 2 enticing games against Hull &amp; Ipswich at the beginning of the season.</li>



<li>His best performances for United came when he came off the bench, and that is what may initially suit him. Plus, with United playing in the Champions League this season, he could be set for more rotation. A wait-and-watch for me at the moment.</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read:</strong> <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-4-5-million-fpl-defenders-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Best £4.5 Million FPL Defenders for the 2026/27 FPL Season</mark></strong></a></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Jean Philippe Mateta – 6.5 Forward &#8211; Crystal Palace</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/mateta-landscape-1024x768.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84926" style="width:739px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/mateta-landscape-1024x768.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/mateta-landscape-300x225.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/mateta-landscape-768x576.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/mateta-landscape-600x450.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/mateta-landscape.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Pros :</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Mateta has slowly become a consistent FPL asset over the last 3 years. 12, 14 and 16 Goals over the last 3 seasons show his reliability. He is also explosive on his day and usually tends to post good underlying numbers throughout the season. He is also on penalties and often plays most of the game when fit.</li>



<li>Palace have some nice games to begin the season with games against Fulham, Ipswich &amp; Leeds in the 1<sup>st</sup> 5 games.</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Cons :</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>What will the departure of Oliver Glasner do to Palace? Is Mateta fully injury-free? These are the answers we need before jumping on the Mateta train in FPL.</li>



<li>Mateta also now has a quality backup behind him with Jorgen Strand Larsen ready to eat into his minutes whenever needed. Unlike Glasner, who had a strong connection with Mateta, Sage will reward the striker spot based on form, and if Mateta struggles initially, he could lose his place. A late return from the World Cup further complicates matters.</li>
</ul>



