<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Sunderland Pre-Season Keynotes:</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Diarra was benched in their last friendly, which should make Le Fee the first-choice penalty taker.</li>



<li><strong>O&#8217;Nien (4.0 defender)</strong> once again started as CB(like in most other games) and is very likely to start GW1 as CB with manager suggesting that Alderete and Mukiele might not be fit to start GW1. But once they are back he will lose this place. So he is a good option only for early Wildcard/GW1 Bench Boost plans. </li>



<li><strong>Hume(4.5 DEF)</strong> is also likely to start as the RB to start the season as seen in the last pre-season game. He&#8217;s got two goals and an assist in pre-season having playing in Right Wing in the earlier pre-season games. </li>



<li>Angulo, who is a £5.0m midfielder in FPL, also seems to be a guaranteed starter</li>
</ul>



