			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Best FPL Midfielders at Each Price Point for the 2026/27 Season</title>
		<link>https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-fpl-midfielders-at-each-price-point-for-the-2026-27-season/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Bakchod FPL]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 19:19:04 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Budget FPL midfielders]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[FPL Midfielders]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Game week Preview]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Ultimate 2026/27 FPL Pre-Season Guide]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Best £4.5 Million FPL Midfielders]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Best £6.5 million FPL Midfielders]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[best 5 million fpl midfielders]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[best 7.5 million fpl midfielders]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[best 8.0 million midfielder fpl]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[best fpl midfielders]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Best FPL Midfielders 2025/26 Season]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[bruno fernandes fpl]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[fpl midfielders analysis]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[FPL midfielders at each price point]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[fpl midfielders comparisons]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[gomez fpl]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Gross FPL]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[le fee fpl]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[mbeumo fpl]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[palmer fpl]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[semenyo fpl]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[szoboszlai fpl]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://allaboutfpl.com/?p=84529</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>In this article, we analyze the Best FPL Midfielders at each price point for the 2026/27 Season with Stats &#038; share our verdict.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-fpl-midfielders-at-each-price-point-for-the-2026-27-season/">Best FPL Midfielders at Each Price Point for the 2026/27 Season</a> appeared first on <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com">ALLABOUTFPL: Your one stop place for all FPL tips, FPL captain picks, FPL news, FPL players, previews, reviews,differential picks, analysis and weekly updates.</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After looking at the <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-fpl-forwards-at-each-price-point-for-the-2026-27-season/" data-type="post" data-id="84528" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">forwards</mark></a></strong>, it&#8217;s time to turn our attention to what is probably the most important position in FPL midfielders. And there is a lot to like this season. At the very top, Bruno Fernandes is in a price bracket of his own at £12.0m.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Just below him, we have Saka and Palmer at £9.5m, while Mbeumo, Cunha, Semenyo and several others give us plenty of options without having to spend premium money. The £7.0m–£8.0m range is particularly interesting, with a mix of established FPL assets, new signings and players who could benefit from a change in role.<br><br>And then we get to the cheaper midfielders. This is where the new defensive contribution points can make a real difference. Players who may previously have been considered too defensive to own can now offer another route to points, while set pieces, penalties and, most importantly, regular minutes can turn a £5.5m midfielder into a very useful FPL asset.<br><br>So, just like with the forwards, I&#8217;ve gone from the highest price point to the lowest, looking at the players who stand out at each level and where I think the best value could be.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>This blog is part of our price point analysis series</strong> written by <strong><a href="https://x.com/BakchodFpl"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">@BakchodFpl</mark></a></strong> (Do give him a follow!)</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-fpl-forwards-at-each-price-point-for-the-2026-27-season/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Best FPL Forwards at Each Price Point for the 2026/27 Season</mark></strong></a></li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/category/ultimate-2026-27-fpl-pre-season-guide/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/category/ultimate-2026-27-fpl-pre-season-guide/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color"><strong>Link to all our 2026/27 Pre-Season articles</strong></mark></a> including all team pre-season friendly updates, best drafts, fixture analysis, position-wise analysis, differentials, players to target, budget enablers and more. Completely free to access as well!</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center">Best FPL Midfielders</h2>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">£12.0m – Bruno Fernandes</h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/b-fernandes-landscape-1024x768.png" alt="Best FPL Midfielders - Bruno Fernandes" class="wp-image-84735" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/b-fernandes-landscape-1024x768.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/b-fernandes-landscape-300x225.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/b-fernandes-landscape-768x576.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/b-fernandes-landscape-600x450.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/b-fernandes-landscape.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There is only one player in this price bracket. <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-premium-fpl-midfielders-8-0-12-0-million-26-27-season/" data-type="post" data-id="84319" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Bruno Fernandes &#8211; £12.0m</mark></a></strong>. And despite the enormous price rise, it is quite difficult to argue that Bruno doesn&#8217;t deserve to be here. He finished 2025/26 with 235 FPL points, just four behind Haaland, after scoring nine goals and providing 24 assists. That was enough to make him the second-highest scoring player in the game.<br><br>But the really interesting part of his season came after Michael Carrick took charge. A change in formation gave Bruno more freedom in the No.10 role, and his FPL output went through the roof. He produced 129 points across the final 17 Gameweeks, making him the highest-scoring player in the game during that period.<br><br>And that role is expected to continue from Gameweek 1. There is also no shortage of routes to points &#8211; penalties, set pieces, assists, goals and regular 90-minute appearances all work in his favour.<br><br>Then there are the opening fixtures. Manchester United begin with Hull and Ipswich, two promoted sides, in their first two Gameweeks. That immediately puts Bruno into the captaincy conversation alongside the likes of Haaland.<br><br>The problem, obviously, is the price. Buying both Haaland and Bruno costs £27.5m, leaving £72.5m for the other 13 players in your squad. That&#8217;s a significant commitment. But if you&#8217;re looking for one midfielder who can genuinely justify a premium price, Bruno is the obvious starting point.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read: <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-2027-fpl-team-structure-guide-with-drafts-ratings/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-2027-fpl-team-structure-guide-with-drafts-ratings/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">FPL Team Structure Guide with Drafts, AI Team Rating, Formations, Pros, Cons and Key Notes</mark></a></strong></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">£9.5m–£10.0m FPL Midfielders – Saka &amp; Palmer</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This is where the decision becomes much more difficult. There are only two players in this bracket, but both have previously shown that they can produce premium-level FPL seasons.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/saka-vs-palmer-1024x768.png" alt="Best FPL Midfielders - Saka &amp; Palmer " class="wp-image-84736" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/saka-vs-palmer-1024x768.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/saka-vs-palmer-300x225.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/saka-vs-palmer-768x576.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/saka-vs-palmer-600x450.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/saka-vs-palmer.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Bukayo Saka – £9.5m</strong></h3>


<img decoding="async" src="https://thumbs.smartframe.io/84d65181a95c24c4fea73e44b4e27a17/ltKDr7o5dBI7.webp?force-scraper=rss&#038;t=rss" alt="SmartFrame Image" />


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Saka is probably the classic &#8220;how much can we trust the minutes?&#8221; player. His 2025/26 season was disrupted by fitness issues, yet he still finished with 157 points. The interesting part is how good his output was whenever he was actually on the pitch.<br><br>Saka&#8217;s points per minute were excellent, and if you extrapolate his output to the sort of minutes played by the top midfielders, his total would have been considerably higher.<br><br>That&#8217;s the reason I don&#8217;t think we should read too much into last season&#8217;s overall ranking. The issue is whether Arsenal can keep him fit and whether they need to manage his minutes more carefully with greater depth across the squad. At £9.5m, that&#8217;s a legitimate concern.<br><br>But if Saka is fully fit and starting regularly, I wouldn&#8217;t be surprised if he quickly becomes one of the most popular midfielders in the game. He&#8217;s a player I&#8217;d rather wait on rather than rule out.</p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Fantasy Football Hub(FFHUB) Free AI Team Rating Tool</mark></a></strong></p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1000" height="596" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84095" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596.png 1000w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596-300x179.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596-768x458.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596-600x358.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px" /></a><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Get your team rated by <strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" data-type="link" data-id="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Fantasy Football Hub</mark></a></strong>&#8216;s AI Team Rating tool for free (Click on the image above to get your team rated).</figcaption></figure>
</div>


<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Cole Palmer – £9.5m</strong></h3>


<img decoding="async" src="https://thumbs.smartframe.io/b0c95bc04383cef69c6b47df872135cf/WmOBClItypFE.webp?force-scraper=rss&#038;t=rss" alt="SmartFrame Image" />


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Palmer is probably the biggest bounce-back candidate in this entire midfield pool. His 2025/26 season was disappointing by his standards, with just 114 FPL points. But we shouldn&#8217;t forget what came before it.<br><br>Palmer had produced back-to-back 200+ point seasons before last year&#8217;s downturn and was the highest-scoring player in FPL in 2023/24. The new season gives him a few reasons for optimism. Chelsea have no European football, Palmer should remain heavily involved in their attack and the arrival of Xabi Alonso provides a fresh tactical setup.<br><br>The price also makes a difference. At £9.5m, he&#8217;s £1.0m cheaper than his starting price last season. So you&#8217;re effectively being asked: Do you believe last season was the new Palmer, or was it simply a bad season? I&#8217;m leaning towards the latter. But I don&#8217;t think Palmer is essential from Gameweek 1, I am instead considering a Bruno Fernandes to Palmer transfer in GW4.<br></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">£8.0m–£8.5m FPL Midfielders – Mbeumo, Cunha, Semenyo &amp; Gibbs-White</h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="209" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-68.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84739" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-68.png 1600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-68-300x39.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-68-1024x134.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-68-768x100.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-68-1536x201.png 1536w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-68-600x78.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1600px) 100vw, 1600px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This is probably my favourite price bracket in midfield. There are four very different players here, and I can see all four becoming popular at different points of the season.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read: <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-27-fpl-chip-strategy-guide-first-half-of-the-season/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-27-fpl-chip-strategy-guide-first-half-of-the-season/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">FPL Chip Strategy Guide- Best Windows to Play Free Hit, Wildcard, Triple Captain and Bench Boost</mark></a></strong></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Bryan Mbeumo – £8.0m</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/mbeumo-vs-cunha-1024x768.png" alt="Best FPL Midfielders - Mbeumo &amp; Cunha" class="wp-image-84738" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/mbeumo-vs-cunha-1024x768.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/mbeumo-vs-cunha-300x225.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/mbeumo-vs-cunha-768x576.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/mbeumo-vs-cunha-600x450.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/mbeumo-vs-cunha.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Mbeumo is my current favourite. The numbers from last season were very encouraging, particularly when you look beyond his final FPL points total. His non-penalty expected goal involvement was among the very best midfielders in the league, while his goal threat was also extremely strong. And then there is the Manchester United factor. Mbeumo has been used centrally during pre-season, which could be a major development from an FPL perspective.<br><br>If he gets a consistent run through the middle, rather than spending most of his time out wide, there is a very obvious route to increased goal involvement. The other attraction is the opening <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/fpl-fixture-analysis-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season-pl-fixtures/" data-type="post" data-id="84047" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">fixture run</mark></a></strong>. Manchester United have Hull and Ipswich in the first two Gameweeks, so there is an immediate opportunity to attack those fixtures.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="784" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-14-at-7.35.04-PM-1-1024x784.png" alt="Best FPL Midfielders - Mbeumo " class="wp-image-84772" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-14-at-7.35.04-PM-1-1024x784.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-14-at-7.35.04-PM-1-300x230.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-14-at-7.35.04-PM-1-768x588.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-14-at-7.35.04-PM-1-600x459.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-14-at-7.35.04-PM-1.png 1176w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There is still competition for places, and I don&#8217;t think we should assume the pre-season role will automatically continue all season. But at £8.0m? Mbeumo is currently my favourite midfielder in this bracket.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read:</strong> <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/ultimate-defcon-analysis-top-players-best-opponents-to-target/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Ultimate DEFCON Analysis: Top Players &amp; Best Opponents to Target</mark></strong></a></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Matheus Cunha – £8.0m</strong></h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cunha gives us another route into the Manchester United attack. He scored 10 goals and provided four assists last season and has now reached double figures for Premier League goals in three consecutive campaigns. The interesting thing about Cunha is his versatility. He can play centrally, from the left or in a deeper attacking role, and that could work particularly well if Mbeumo is given the central role.<br><br>So while I currently prefer Mbeumo, I don&#8217;t think the gap is particularly large.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Antoine Semenyo – £8.5m</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/semenyo-landscape-1024x768.png" alt="Best FPL Midfielders - Semenyo " class="wp-image-84740" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/semenyo-landscape-1024x768.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/semenyo-landscape-300x225.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/semenyo-landscape-768x576.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/semenyo-landscape-600x450.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/semenyo-landscape.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Semenyo comes off a season where he produced 17 goals and six assists, which is excellent output at any price. He had 202 FPL points last season. Now put him as a winger into a City attack under Maresca and the ceiling becomes very interesting. The problem is obvious &#8211; Manchester City minutes.<br><br>There are plenty of attacking options competing for places, and we don&#8217;t yet have enough evidence to know exactly how the preferred XI will look. Semenyo&#8217;s position is also worth monitoring.<br><br>If he is consistently playing in an advanced wide role and starting regularly, £8.5m could prove to be very good value. If rotation becomes an issue, however, the price becomes much harder to justify. High ceiling, but I want more certainty on minutes.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Morgan Gibbs-White – £8.0m</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gibbs-white-landscape-1024x768.png" alt="Best FPL Midfielders - Gibbs White " class="wp-image-84741" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gibbs-white-landscape-1024x768.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gibbs-white-landscape-300x225.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gibbs-white-landscape-768x576.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gibbs-white-landscape-600x450.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gibbs-white-landscape.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Gibbs-White is another player I really like, but probably not immediately. He had a superb 2025/26 season, finishing with 15 goals and 188 FPL points. That put him among the highest-scoring midfielders in the game.<br><br>The problem is Forest&#8217;s fixture run. They start with Leeds, but then have Liverpool, Tottenham, Aston Villa and Arsenal in the early part of the season. That&#8217;s enough to make me hold fire.<br><br>But I absolutely want him on the watchlist. If Forest&#8217;s attack looks good and the fixtures improve, Gibbs-White at £8.0m could become a very strong option.</p>



