<h3 class="wp-block-heading">£7.5m FPL Midfielders – Wirtz, Rice, Cherki &amp; Rogers</h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="209" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-70.png" alt="Best FPL Midfielders - Wirtz, Rice, Rogers, Cherki " class="wp-image-84743" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-70.png 1600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-70-300x39.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-70-1024x134.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-70-768x100.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-70-1536x201.png 1536w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-70-600x78.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1600px) 100vw, 1600px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This is another price point where there are several interesting options, but for completely different reasons.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Florian Wirtz – £7.5m</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/wirtz-landscape-1024x768.png" alt="Best FPL Midfielders - Wirtz" class="wp-image-84744" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/wirtz-landscape-1024x768.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/wirtz-landscape-300x225.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/wirtz-landscape-768x576.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/wirtz-landscape-600x450.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/wirtz-landscape.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><br><br>Wirtz is probably my favourite <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/most-fpl-points-scored-by-players-in-an-fpl-gameweek-fpl-history/" data-type="post" data-id="20996" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">£7.5m midfielder</mark></a></strong>. His first season at Liverpool wasn&#8217;t spectacular by his standards. He finished with five goals and four assists from 27 starts, which is fine but not what you would expect from a player of his reputation.<br><br>The interesting part is what happens next. With a new manager and Salah no longer at Liverpool, Wirtz could have a much more important role in the attack. If he is used centrally and consistently gets into the areas where he can influence goals, I think there is plenty of room for improvement.<br><br>And the price helps. He started 2025/26 at £8.5m and is now available for £7.5m, so the market is already pricing in a significant drop in expectations. For me, this is exactly the sort of player worth taking a calculated gamble on. Wirtz is my £7.5m pick.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read: <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/fpl-rotational-pairs-combinations-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/fpl-rotational-pairs-combinations-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">FPL Rotational Pairs and Combinations for 2026/27 FPL Season</mark></a></strong></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Declan Rice – £7.5m</strong></h3>


<img decoding="async" src="https://thumbs.smartframe.io/1ffbae35d432d0d71911ca2a0b209fbb/prsiAuqugrot.webp?force-scraper=rss&#038;t=rss" alt="SmartFrame Image" />


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Rice is the safer option. He doesn&#8217;t have the explosive attacking ceiling of Wirtz, but his FPL profile is much more about accumulating points from several different sources. He finished 2025/26 with 184 points, helped by four goals, nine assists and his ability to pick up defensive contribution points.<br><br>That makes him particularly interesting at £7.5m. The main issue is fitness. If he comes into the season fully fit and remains a regular starter, Rice can be one of those players who quietly keeps ticking along without needing huge hauls. But if I&#8217;m spending £7.5m on a midfielder, I would probably prefer a little more attacking upside.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read: <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/eight-simple-fpl-tips-to-secure-a-high-rank-26-27-season/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Eight Simple FPL Tips to Secure a High Rank | 26/27 Season</mark></a></strong></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Rayan Cherki – £7.5m</strong></h3>


<img decoding="async" src="https://thumbs.smartframe.io/0b629b85ba2abe5ff39df9829ee5fb57/mcfcNOYwR2NN.webp?force-scraper=rss&#038;t=rss" alt="SmartFrame Image" />


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cherki is one of the more exciting City options. He managed four goals and 13 assists from only 19 starts last season, so the creative potential is obvious. The problem is the same one we have with Semenyo &#8211; minutes. With Foden, Semenyo, Doku and several other attacking players competing for minutes, it&#8217;s difficult to project Cherki&#8217;s starts with confidence.<br><br>That&#8217;s particularly important at £7.5m. If he becomes a regular starter, I&#8217;d be very interested. Until then, watchlist.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read: <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/fpl-fixture-analysis-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season-pl-fixtures/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/fpl-fixture-analysis-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season-pl-fixtures/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">FPL Fixture Analysis for 2026/27 Season- Teams with Best and Worst fixtures</mark></a></strong></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Morgan Rogers – £7.5m</strong></h3>


<img decoding="async" src="https://thumbs.smartframe.io/04742eb90cefa12a5e3ab9bae92c2b93/neimOganIoE6.webp?force-scraper=rss&#038;t=rss" alt="SmartFrame Image" />


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Rogers has quietly become one of the most interesting mid-priced midfielders. He produced 10 goals and eight assists last season and has shown good availability over the last couple of campaigns. Now he gets a fresh challenge at Chelsea. The obvious attraction is playing alongside Palmer.<br><br>If Alonso can get Rogers into advanced positions regularly, there is enough attacking quality here to make £7.5m look very reasonable. I wouldn&#8217;t be surprised if Rogers becomes one of those players who starts the season under the radar and ends up in a lot of teams.</p>



