<h3 class="wp-block-heading">£7.0m FPL Midfielders – Szoboszlai, Foden, Enzo, Gakpo &amp; Bruno Guimarães</h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="184" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-71.png" alt="Best £7.0m FPL Midfielders Analysis – Szoboszlai, Foden, Enzo, Gakpo &amp; Bruno Guimarães" class="wp-image-84747" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-71.png 1600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-71-300x35.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-71-1024x118.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-71-768x88.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-71-1536x177.png 1536w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-71-600x69.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1600px) 100vw, 1600px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This is another price point with plenty of potential.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Dominik Szoboszlai – £7.0m</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/szoboszlai-landscape-1024x768.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84749" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/szoboszlai-landscape-1024x768.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/szoboszlai-landscape-300x225.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/szoboszlai-landscape-768x576.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/szoboszlai-landscape-600x450.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/szoboszlai-landscape.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This is probably my favourite £7.0m midfielder. Szoboszlai started 36 of Liverpool&#8217;s 38 league matches last season, which is a huge attraction at this price. He finished with six goals and seven assists, while also collecting defensive contribution points. Add in set-piece involvement and the potential for regular 90-minute appearances and you have a midfielder with several different ways of returning.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-19-2-1024x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84774" style="width:510px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-19-2-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-19-2-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-19-2-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-19-2-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-19-2-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-19-2.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The big question is his exact role. With Wirtz around, Szoboszlai could spend more time deeper in midfield. But Liverpool&#8217;s opening <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/fpl-fixture-analysis-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season-pl-fixtures/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/fpl-fixture-analysis-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season-pl-fixtures/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">fixtures</mark></a></strong> are excellent. And at £7.0m, I don&#8217;t need Szoboszlai to become an explosive midfielder. If he keeps starting every week, he can simply be a very good FPL asset.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read: </strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-fpl-gw1-drafts-for-the-26-27-fpl-season-with-pros-cons/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Best FPL GW1 Drafts for the 26/27 FPL Season with Pros &amp; Cons</mark></strong></a></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Phil Foden – £7.0m</strong></h3>


<img decoding="async" src="https://thumbs.smartframe.io/0b629b85ba2abe5ff39df9829ee5fb57/mcfcq7PO9UqO.webp?force-scraper=rss&#038;t=rss" alt="SmartFrame Image" />


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Foden at £7.0m feels strange.<br><br>Three seasons ago, he scored 19 Premier League goals and 8 assists. Last season, he managed 7 goals and 5 assists. That&#8217;s the kind of difference that makes him one of the biggest potential value picks in the game. If Foden gets a consistent run of starts, £7.0m could prove to be an enormous bargain.<br><br>The obvious issue is, once again like all Manchester City players, minutes. City have enough attacking talent to make almost every midfielder in their squad a rotation risk. So I&#8217;m interested in Foden. I&#8217;m just not prepared to assume that a cheap price automatically means nailed minutes. He is one of the biggest upside picks in this price bracket though.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read:</strong> <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-27-fpl-chip-strategy-guide-first-half-of-the-season/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-27-fpl-chip-strategy-guide-first-half-of-the-season/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">FPL Chip Strategy Guide- Best Windows to Play Free Hit, Wildcard, Triple Captain and Bench Boost</mark></a></strong></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Enzo Fernández – £7.0m</strong></h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Enzo could have probably been the more reliable Chelsea option, but will he stay at Chelsea or move to Manchester City &#8211; that&#8217;s the key question. He finished 2025/26 with 157 FPL points and was Chelsea&#8217;s highest-scoring midfielder. His underlying numbers were also strong. At £7.0m, that makes him interesting.<br><br>The question is how Alonso uses him if he stays at Chelsea or how Maresca will use him, should he move to Manchester City. If he plays further forward, the appeal increases considerably. If he drops deeper, his ceiling falls. So this is another one where role and team structure (wherever he does end up playing) matters almost as much as the player.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read: </strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/ultimate-defcon-analysis-top-players-best-opponents-to-target/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Ultimate DEFCON Analysis: Top Players &amp; Best Opponents to Target</mark></strong></a></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Cody Gakpo – £7.0m</strong></h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Gakpo is an interesting option simply because of what he has already shown in the Premier League. He can play through the middle or from the left and has demonstrated that he can contribute goals and assists. But Liverpool&#8217;s attacking structure is changing and there remains some uncertainty around his exact role. There are also rumours of him moving to Tottenham. For now, I wouldn&#8217;t make him a priority. But if the role becomes clearer, £7.0m could be a very attractive price.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Bruno Guimarães – £7.0m</strong></h3>


<img decoding="async" src="https://thumbs.smartframe.io/c78749ece7fd074ea5dc1889e7c53f0f/esmeAJ71IQpw.webp?force-scraper=rss&#038;t=rss" alt="SmartFrame Image" />


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Bruno Guimarães is another player whose FPL appeal depends heavily on his role. He comes off a season where he produced nine goals and seven assists for Newcastle despite playing only 26 matches.<br><br>Now at Arsenal, there is plenty of talent around him. The question is whether that helps or hurts his FPL prospects. If he&#8217;s given a more attacking role, there is obvious appeal. If he becomes another deeper midfielder in the Arsenal system, I&#8217;d rather look elsewhere. One to monitor rather than buy blindly.</p>



