<h3 class="wp-block-heading">£6.5m FPL Midfielders – Tzolis, Sarr, Wilson, Anderson &amp; Dewsbury-Hall</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This could be one of the most important price points for squad structure. There are several players here who can potentially give you premium-level returns without premium-level prices.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="446" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-73.png" alt="Best £6.5m FPL Midfielders Analysis – Tzolis, Sarr, Wilson, Anderson &amp; Dewsbury-Hall" class="wp-image-84754" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-73.png 1600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-73-300x84.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-73-1024x285.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-73-768x214.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-73-1536x428.png 1536w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-73-600x167.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1600px) 100vw, 1600px" /></figure>
</div>


<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Christos Tzolis – £6.5m</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-76-1024x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84770" style="width:594px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-76-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-76-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-76-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-76-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-76-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-76.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><br><strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-fpl-value-midfielders-to-consider-for-the-2026-27-season/" data-type="post" data-id="84517" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Tzolis</mark></a></strong> is probably the biggest differential and my favourite pick in this bucket. He arrives with an excellent record from Belgium and has looked very good during pre-season. The most important question is whether Arsenal actually give him enough minutes.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If he starts Gameweek 1 and the role looks secure, I think the interest will be immediate. At £6.5m, you don&#8217;t need him to become Saka. You just need him to be an attacking midfielder playing regularly for Arsenal. If the minutes are there, I&#8217;m interested.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Ismaïla Sarr – £6.5m</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/sarr-landscape-1024x768.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84751" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/sarr-landscape-1024x768.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/sarr-landscape-300x225.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/sarr-landscape-768x576.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/sarr-landscape-600x450.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/sarr-landscape.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sarr is the sort of midfielder who can quietly become very useful. He scored nine goals last season and also had a very strong big-chance profile despite not playing as many minutes as some of the other players around him. His positioning is particularly interesting.<br><br>He was often operating closer to Mateta rather than simply hugging the touchline, which gives him more goal threat. Palace&#8217;s fixtures also improve after the opening couple of Gameweeks. So Sarr could be one of those players where the Gameweek 1 decision isn&#8217;t obvious, but the Gameweek 3 decision is. Palace play FUL (A), IPS (H) and LEE (A) from GW3-5.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read:</strong> <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-2027-fpl-team-structure-guide-with-drafts-ratings/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-2027-fpl-team-structure-guide-with-drafts-ratings/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">FPL Team Structure Guide with Drafts, AI Team Rating, Formations, Pros, Cons and Key Notes</mark></a></strong></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Harry Wilson – £6.5m</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-18-1-1024x1024.png" alt="Best £6.5m FPL Midfielder – Harry Wilson" class="wp-image-84769" style="width:606px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-18-1-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-18-1-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-18-1-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-18-1-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-18-1-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-18-1.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Wilson is one of my favourite options in this price range. He produced 10 goals and nine assists for Fulham last season and finished with 168 FPL points. Now he gets a move to Leeds, where the early <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/fpl-fixture-analysis-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season-pl-fixtures/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">fixture run </mark></strong></a>is very appealing. Leeds don&#8217;t face one of last season&#8217;s big six until Gameweek 6, and there are three home matches among the first five.<br><br>The obvious concern is regression. His underlying numbers weren&#8217;t quite as strong as the final output suggests. But at £6.5m, I don&#8217;t need him to repeat 19 attacking returns. If he starts regularly, he has a very good chance of being one of the best-value midfielders in the opening Gameweeks.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read:</strong> <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-fpl-forwards-at-each-price-point-for-the-2026-27-season/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-fpl-forwards-at-each-price-point-for-the-2026-27-season/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Top Forwards at every price point for the 2026/27 FPL Season</mark></a></strong></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Elliot Anderson – £6.5m</strong></h3>


<img decoding="async" src="https://thumbs.smartframe.io/0b629b85ba2abe5ff39df9829ee5fb57/mcfcJghzYpZm.webp?force-scraper=rss&#038;t=rss" alt="SmartFrame Image" />


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Anderson is a fascinating example of how defensive contribution points have changed the midfield landscape. He scored only four goals and provided five assists last season. Yet he still finished with 180 FPL points. How? Defensive contributions. <strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color"><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/ultimate-defcon-analysis-top-players-best-opponents-to-target/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">52 DC points last season</a></mark></strong>. He was among the best midfielders in the game for these points at Forest.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The challenge is that he now plays for Manchester City. City dominate possession, so he won&#8217;t get the same volume of defensive actions that he had at Forest. That makes his new role absolutely crucial. If he&#8217;s playing regularly, he&#8217;s interesting. But I wouldn&#8217;t buy him expecting last season&#8217;s defensive numbers to simply repeat themselves.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read:</strong> <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-6m-forwards-comparison-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Best £6m Forwards Comparison for the 2026/27 FPL Season</mark></a></strong></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Kiernan Dewsbury-Hall – £6.5m</strong></h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Dewsbury-Hall is probably the least exciting but safest option in this bracket. He produced eight goals and seven assists for Everton last season and was extremely reliable for minutes. He also has some set-piece involvement and can pick up defensive contribution points. Everton&#8217;s early fixtures are favourable too. He may not give you many explosive hauls. But at £6.5m, he could simply keep ticking along.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">£6.0m FPL Midfielders – Schade, Le Fée, Tavernier &amp; Kluivert</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This is where I start getting very interested.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="785" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-74.png" alt="Best £6.0m FPL Midfielders Analysis – Schade, Le Fée, Tavernier &amp; Kluivert" class="wp-image-84755" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-74.png 1600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-74-300x147.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-74-1024x502.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-74-768x377.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-74-1536x754.png 1536w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-74-600x294.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1600px) 100vw, 1600px" /></figure>
</div>


<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Kevin Schade – £6.0m</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/schade-landscape-1024x768.png" alt="Best £6.0m FPL Midfielders - Schade" class="wp-image-84756" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/schade-landscape-1024x768.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/schade-landscape-300x225.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/schade-landscape-768x576.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/schade-landscape-600x450.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/schade-landscape.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Schade&#8217;s numbers are probably too good for us to ignore. He finished with eight goals and five assists, but his underlying numbers suggest that there could be more to come. His xG was the highest among midfielders in this price range, while he also ranked extremely highly for big chances and shots inside the box.<br><br>And then look at the opening fixtures: Spurs (H), Leeds (A), Sunderland (H), Bournemouth (A).<br><br>That&#8217;s a very appealing start. The issue is minutes. Schade was regularly substituted last season, so even when he starts, he isn&#8217;t necessarily guaranteed a full 90. Still, at £6.0m, he&#8217;s one of the more exciting budget midfielders.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read:</strong> <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-fpl-budget-forwards-4-5-6-0-million-26-27-fpl-season/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Best FPL Budget Forwards (£4.5 &#8211; £6.0 Million) | 26/27 FPL Season</mark></strong></a></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Enzo Le Fée – £6.0m</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="328" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-14-at-7.29.37-PM-1-1024x328.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84768" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-14-at-7.29.37-PM-1-1024x328.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-14-at-7.29.37-PM-1-300x96.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-14-at-7.29.37-PM-1-768x246.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-14-at-7.29.37-PM-1-600x192.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-14-at-7.29.37-PM-1.png 1192w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Le Fee Stats </figcaption></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Le Fée is another player I really like. He had six goals and six assists last season, while also adding defensive contribution points. He&#8217;s involved in set pieces and could have some responsibility from penalties. Most importantly, he looks like the sort of player who can play a lot of minutes.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sunderland&#8217;s opening run is also attractive &#8211; Ipswich, Fulham and Brentford are the first three. At £6.0m, that&#8217;s enough to make him one of my favourite budget picks.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read:</strong> <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-fpl-value-defenders-and-gks-for-the-2026-27-season/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/fpl-rotational-pairs-combinations-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Best Value for Money Defenders and GKs for 2026/27 FPL season</mark></a></strong></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Marcus Tavernier &amp; Justin Kluivert – £6.0m</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/tavernier-vs-kluivert-1024x768.png" alt="Best £6.0m FPL Midfielders - Tavernier, Kluivert" class="wp-image-84757" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/tavernier-vs-kluivert-1024x768.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/tavernier-vs-kluivert-300x225.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/tavernier-vs-kluivert-768x576.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/tavernier-vs-kluivert-600x450.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/tavernier-vs-kluivert.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Bournemouth&#8217;s midfield options are interesting, but I&#8217;m not rushing into them. Kluivert has already provided a reminder of his goal threat during pre-season, while Tavernier offers another route through set pieces and attacking involvement.<br><br>The big question is penalties. If one of them becomes the clear penalty taker, the equation changes. But with Bournemouth&#8217;s opening fixtures being less attractive, I&#8217;d rather monitor the situation. Kluivert is the one I&#8217;d keep the closest eye on.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read:</strong> <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-4-5-million-fpl-defenders-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Best £4.5 Million FPL Defenders for the 2026/27 FPL Season</mark></a></strong></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">£5.5m FPL Midfielders – Groß, Sangaré, Ampadu &amp; Xhaka</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This is where the defensive contribution points become particularly useful.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="991" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-75.png" alt="Best £5.5m FPL Midfielders Analysis – Groß, Sangaré, Ampadu &amp; Xhaka" class="wp-image-84759" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-75.png 1600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-75-300x186.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-75-1024x634.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-75-768x476.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-75-1536x951.png 1536w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-75-600x372.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1600px) 100vw, 1600px" /></figure>
</div>


<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Pascal Groß – £5.5m</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gro-landscape-1-1024x768.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84758" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gro-landscape-1-1024x768.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gro-landscape-1-300x225.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gro-landscape-1-768x576.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gro-landscape-1-600x450.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gro-landscape-1.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Groß is probably the first name I&#8217;d look at. He returned to Brighton midway through last season and immediately became a regular, with excellent minutes. He brings set pieces, creativity and defensive contributions.<br><br>But the biggest question is penalties. If Groß takes them following Welbeck&#8217;s departure, £5.5m starts looking very attractive. The only concerns are his age and the additional European schedule. For now though, he&#8217;s firmly on my shortlist.</p>



