<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Mamadou Sangaré – £5.5m</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-9-1024x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84406" style="width:598px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-9-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-9-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-9-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-9-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-9-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-9.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sangaré is the more aggressive punt. You&#8217;re not buying him because you expect 10 goals. You&#8217;re buying him because he could collect a lot of defensive contribution points. His defensive numbers were excellent last season, and he also chipped in with some attacking returns.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="310" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-14-at-7.27.05-PM-1024x310.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84766" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-14-at-7.27.05-PM-1024x310.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-14-at-7.27.05-PM-300x91.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-14-at-7.27.05-PM-768x233.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-14-at-7.27.05-PM-600x182.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screenshot-2026-08-14-at-7.27.05-PM.png 1156w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The challenge is translating that into the Premier League. If he is nailed, however, he could be exactly the type of <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-fpl-value-midfielders-to-consider-for-the-2026-27-season/" data-type="post" data-id="84517" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">£5.5m midfielder </mark></a></strong>that helps make an expensive squad structure work.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Ethan Ampadu – £5.5m</strong></h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ampadu is another reliable option. He started 35 matches last season and frequently hit the defensive contribution threshold. The attacking upside isn&#8217;t huge, but that isn&#8217;t really the point. At £5.5m, if he is starting every week and regularly picking up defensive contribution points, he can do a job. A boring FPL pick can sometimes be a very good FPL pick.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read:</strong> <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/fpl-rotational-pairs-combinations-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/fpl-rotational-pairs-combinations-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">FPL Rotational Pairs and Combinations for 2026/27 FPL Season</mark></a></strong></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Granit Xhaka – £5.5m</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="819" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/xhaka-1024x819.webp" alt="" class="wp-image-84388" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/xhaka-1024x819.webp 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/xhaka-300x240.webp 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/xhaka-768x614.webp 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/xhaka-600x480.webp 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/xhaka.webp 1200w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><br><br>Xhaka offers a similar profile. He is likely to get plenty of minutes, contributes defensively and can provide the occasional goal or assist. The opening Sunderland fixtures are also favourable. I don&#8217;t expect many 12-point hauls. But if you&#8217;re looking for a midfielder who can sit on your bench or rotate into your XI without worrying about minutes, Xhaka makes sense.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read: <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/best-5-0-5-5-million-fpl-defenders-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Best £5.0-5.5 Million FPL Defenders for the 2026/27 FPL Season</mark></a></strong></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">£5.0m FPL Midfielders – Diego Gómez &amp; Christian Nørgaard</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There aren&#8217;t many obvious £5.0m options. But two names stand out.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gomez-vs-n-rgaard-1024x768.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84760" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gomez-vs-n-rgaard-1024x768.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gomez-vs-n-rgaard-300x225.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gomez-vs-n-rgaard-768x576.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gomez-vs-n-rgaard-600x450.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/gomez-vs-n-rgaard.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Diego Gómez – £5.0m</strong></h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Gómez is the more exciting option and my favourite pick from this bucket. He scored five goals and added an assist last season while also producing good defensive numbers. The big attraction is the possibility of him getting a regular attacking role.<br>If Brighton give him a consistent starting position, £5.0m becomes very difficult to ignore. One to monitor closely before Gameweek 1.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read:</strong> <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/best-premium-fpl-defenders-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/best-premium-fpl-defenders-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Best Premium Defenders for 2026/27 season based on Stats and Fixtures</mark></a></strong></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Christian Nørgaard – £5.0m</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-17-1-1024x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84765" style="width:485px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-17-1-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-17-1-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-17-1-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-17-1-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-17-1-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-17-1.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Nørgaard is a very different option. His appeal comes almost entirely from minutes and his ability to pick up points through multiple routes. His numbers in Brentford in 2024-25 included five goals and four assists, alongside a decent defensive contribution record. He moved to Arsenal last season but played only 106 minutes, which is probably why he decided to move to Everton this season. If Everton make him a regular starter, he could comfortably outperform his £5.0m price.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read:</strong> <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/best-4-0-million-fpl-defenders-for-2026-27-fpl-season/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Best £4.0 Million FPL Defenders for 2026/27 FPL Season</mark></strong></a></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">£4.5m – The Enablers</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">And finally, we get to the £4.5m midfielders. This is where I don&#8217;t think we need to force an answer yet. The main thing we&#8217;re looking for here is a player who starts regularly.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Slater is one of the safer options from a minutes perspective. Matt Crooks offers a little more attacking potential. Yates is another player whose defensive contribution numbers make him interesting.<br><br>There are others who could emerge as the season gets closer. But at this price, I would rather wait for the team sheets than pick someone simply because he&#8217;s cheap. If one of these players nails down a starting role, that&#8217;s when the calculation changes. For now, there isn&#8217;t a clear £4.5m midfielder I want to lock into my squad.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read:</strong> <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-fpl-goalkeepers-to-target-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-fpl-goalkeepers-to-target-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Best FPL Goalkeepers to Target based on Stats and Fixtures</mark></a></strong></p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center"><strong>My Current Favourite FPL Midfielder at Each Price Point</strong></h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If I had to pick one midfielder from each bracket right now, my shortlist would look like this:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>£12.0m &#8211; </strong>Bruno Fernandes</li>



<li><strong>£9.5m &#8211;</strong> Palmer</li>



<li><strong>£8.5m &#8211;</strong> Antoine Semenyo</li>



<li><strong>£8.0m &#8211;</strong> Bryan Mbeumo</li>



<li><strong>£7.5m &#8211; </strong>Florian Wirtz</li>



<li><strong>£7.0m &#8211;</strong> Dominik Szoboszlai</li>



<li><strong>£6.5m &#8211;</strong> Christos Tzolis</li>



<li><strong>£6.0m &#8211; </strong>Enzo Le Fée</li>



<li><strong>£5.5m &#8211;</strong> Pascal Groß</li>



<li><strong>£5.0m &#8211; </strong>Diego Gómez</li>



<li><strong>£4.5m &#8211;</strong> No clear standout yet</li>
</ul>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Conclusion</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The midfield position is probably where we will see the biggest difference between FPL squads this season.<br><br>At the top, Bruno Fernandes is expensive, but there is a reason for it. He finished just four points behind Haaland last season and then became the highest-scoring player in the game after Carrick took over. Add penalties, set pieces and the opening fixtures, and there is a very strong case for him despite the £12.0m price tag.<br><br>Then things get much more interesting. Saka and Palmer both have the pedigree to justify £9.5m, but both come with different questions after difficult 2025/26 campaigns. At £8.0m, I currently prefer Mbeumo, particularly because of his potential central role at Manchester United and their excellent opening fixtures. But Cunha is right there, while Semenyo at £8.5m gives us an intriguing route into Manchester City&#8217;s attack.<br><br>Then we have the £7.5m–£7.0m range. Wirtz and Szoboszlai are the two players I&#8217;m most interested in here. Wirtz is a bet on a new role and improved output at Liverpool, while Szoboszlai offers something slightly different &#8211; regular minutes, set pieces and defensive contribution points.<br><br>And then comes the value. Wilson, Tzolis, Schade and Le Fée all have genuine potential to outperform their prices. That is probably the biggest theme I&#8217;ve taken from going through the midfielders.<br><br>You don&#8217;t necessarily need to find the next Palmer. You need to find players who have enough different ways of scoring FPL points to justify their price.<br><br>A midfielder with penalties is valuable. A midfielder on set pieces is valuable. A midfielder who plays 90 minutes every week is valuable. And now, a midfielder who regularly hits the defensive contribution threshold can be valuable too.<br><br>That&#8217;s why I wouldn&#8217;t simply rank these players by goals and assists from last season.<br><br>Look at role, minutes, fixtures and routes to points.<br><br>Because in a season where Haaland and Bruno alone can cost you £27.5m, finding the right value in midfield could be the difference between a squad that feels impossible to build and one that has genuine depth across all 15 players.</p>



