</div><p>The post <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-fpl-midfielders-at-each-price-point-for-the-2026-27-season/">Best FPL Midfielders at Each Price Point for the 2026/27 Season</a> appeared first on <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com">ALLABOUTFPL: Your one stop place for all FPL tips, FPL captain picks, FPL news, FPL players, previews, reviews,differential picks, analysis and weekly updates.</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Best FPL Value Defenders and GKs for the 2026/27 Season</title>
		<link>https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-fpl-value-defenders-and-gks-for-the-2026-27-season/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[aww.soum]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 19:56:02 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[FPL Budget Defenders]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[FPL Defenders]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Game week Preview]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Ultimate 2026/27 FPL Pre-Season Guide]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[best budget defenders]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[best budget goalkeepers]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[best value defenders]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[best value goalkeepers]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[FPL budget defenders]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[FPL Defenders to Target]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[FPL GW1 Defenders]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[fpl gw1 goalkeepers]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[fpl value defenders for 2026/27 season]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[gameweek 1 defenders]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[top budget picks for fpl gw1]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[top defenders for fpl gw1]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[top value defenders for 2026/27 season]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://allaboutfpl.com/?p=84720</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>In this article, we look at some of the Best Value Defenders and GKs based on Stats and Fixtures whose price tags look generous.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-fpl-value-defenders-and-gks-for-the-2026-27-season/">Best FPL Value Defenders and GKs for the 2026/27 Season</a> appeared first on <a href="https://allaboutfpl.com">ALLABOUTFPL: Your one stop place for all FPL tips, FPL captain picks, FPL news, FPL players, previews, reviews,differential picks, analysis and weekly updates.</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In the previous two articles, we had covered the engine of your FPL team (midfielders) and had looked at the turbo boost that can take it from good to great (forwards). Now, it’s time to focus on the heart of the team – the defence (defenders &amp; goalkeepers).</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There is a famous footballing philosophy, often attributed to Sir Alex Ferguson: “Attack wins you games, defence wins you titles.”</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">And while FPL isn&#8217;t quite the same as football, there is plenty of truth in that philosophy when it comes to building a squad for a 38-game season. The flashy attackers might grab the headlines, but a reliable defence can quietly rack up points week after week – clean sheets, defensive contributions, saves, bonus points and the occasional attacking return.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">More importantly, getting the defence right is what allows you to spend big elsewhere. A £4.5m defender/ goalkeeper who consistently delivers can be far more valuable to your squad in more ways than one by enabling another premium asset in your XI and at the same time keeping your points tally ticking.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">With the deadline fast approaching, let&#8217;s complete our search for value by looking at the budget goalkeepers and defenders who could form the backbone of your FPL team this season.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">So, hello and welcome to the last article of this series where we continue our search for value picks – this time, turning our attention to the defenders and goalkeepers. So, let&#8217;s start the article for this GW, sponsored by …. Well, nobody. We are poor, but you can help <a href="https://www.buymeacoffee.com/allaboutfpl">here</a> if you want. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/category/ultimate-2026-27-fpl-pre-season-guide/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/category/ultimate-2026-27-fpl-pre-season-guide/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color"><strong>Link to all our 2026/27 Pre-Season articles</strong></mark></a> including all team pre-season friendly updates, best drafts, fixture analysis, position-wise analysis, differentials, players to target, budget enablers and more. Completely free to access as well!</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center">Top Value Defenders and Goal Keepers to Target for 2026/27 season</h2>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Brighton Bravados</strong></h3>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Bart Verbruggen (£4.5m) – GKP, Brighton – 18.0% TSB</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-22-1024x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84730" style="width:616px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-22-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-22-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-22-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-22-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-22-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-22.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Verbruggenis a hot property sitting in 18% teams. And there’s solid reason for that.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He was the highest scoring GKP priced £4.5m or lower and faces Leeds and Coventry in the first 5 GWs. They also face Chelsea against who Brighton conceded just 1 goal and scored 6 in the two fixtures, the last being a Clean Sheet by Verbruggen.<br>Brighton also conceded the 3<sup>rd</sup> least goals in the league last season. Verbruggen can well be your set and forget budget GKP for the season.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">PS – I am aware of the community interest in Kinský. But I am not too convinced with Spurs defence – they conceded the most goals among the 17 non-relegated EPL teams. They’ve lost their rock Romero and not sure how Senesi and Van Hecke will link up with Micky and Porro/ Robertson.</p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Fantasy Football Hub(FFHUB) Free AI Team Rating Tool</mark></a></strong></p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1000" height="596" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84095" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596.png 1000w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596-300x179.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596-768x458.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_GYTR_1000x596-600x358.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px" /></a><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Get your team rated by <strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" data-type="link" data-id="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/ai-team-rating?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=team-rating&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Fantasy Football Hub</mark></a></strong>&#8216;s AI Team Rating tool for free (Click on the image above to get your team rated).</figcaption></figure>
</div>


<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Luka Vušković (£5.0m) – DEF, Brighton – 2.7% TSB</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-19-1024x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84728" style="width:656px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-19-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-19-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-19-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-19-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-19-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-19.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Vuskovic could be one of those £5.0m defenders who makes a mockery of his price tag. His numbers from last season already make for interesting reading: a <strong>63% DEFCON hit rate and 12.4 defensive contributions per start,</strong> alongside six attacking returns. So there is a fairly strong defensive floor, but what makes him particularly exciting is the potential at the other end.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Brighton’s set-piece threat could be the key. Against Roma, Vuskovic played just 45 minutes but still managed 6 DEFCON and an effort from a corner. More importantly, he was repeatedly getting on the end of Pascal Groß&#8217;s deliveries, suggesting that the attacking returns may not be merely theoretical. If he can establish himself as a regular target from corners, his combination of DEFCON and goal threat could make £5.0m look very cheap indeed.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The obvious – and rather significant – question is minutes. I want to see enough evidence that Vuskovic is nailed before putting him into my GW1 squad. If that box gets ticked, though, the fixtures make the proposition even more attractive: Leeds (H) in GW3 and Coventry (A) in GW4, followed by Sunderland (A) in GW6. Brighton also rotate beautifully with Manchester United, potentially giving you a very appealing defensive run by alternating Vuskovic with a United defender. If the minutes are secure, Vuskovic could be one of the most exciting £5.0m defenders to start the season.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read: </strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/fpl-rotational-pairs-combinations-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">FPL Rotational Pairs &amp; Combinations for the 2026/27 FPL Season</mark></strong></a></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Manchester Magicians</strong></h3>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Senne Lammens (£5.0m) – GKP, Man Utd – 19.7% TSB</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-20-1024x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84729" style="width:638px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-20-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-20-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-20-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-20-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-20-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-20.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Senne Lammens arrived at Manchester United last summer for just £18m, relatively unknown to most Premier League fans. Twelve months later, he has gone from an intriguing prospect to United’s undisputed No.1 – and his debut Premier League season was quite something. Lammens lost just four of 32 league games, prevented 6.5 goals, the most of any goalkeeper in the league, and was even named Premier League Signing of the Season.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For FPL, his numbers are equally encouraging. Lammens finished last season with 109 points at 3.4 points per game, while his 11 bonus points were bettered by only one goalkeeper, Roefs (12). That is particularly interesting for a goalkeeper who isn&#8217;t solely reliant on clean sheets to deliver points. His shot-stopping ability gives him a route to save points and bonus even when United fail to keep the opposition out.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">And then there is the fixture list. Manchester United couldn&#8217;t have asked for a better start, facing Hull (A) and Ipswich (H) – the two promoted sides – in the opening two Gameweeks. With Lammens now firmly established as United&#8217;s first-choice goalkeeper and a kind opening schedule, he looks like a very strong option for managers looking for a £5.0m goalkeeper who can deliver both save-based points and clean-sheet potential.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The big question isn&#8217;t whether Lammens can perform. It&#8217;s whether United can give him enough clean sheets to turn those impressive individual numbers into elite FPL returns.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read: </strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/2026-2027-fpl-team-structure-guide-with-drafts-ratings/"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">2026/2027 FPL Team Structure Guide with Drafts &amp; Ratings</mark></strong></a></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Luke Shaw (£4.5m) – DEF, Man Utd – 24.3% TSB</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-17-1024x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84725" style="width:666px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-17-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-17-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-17-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-17-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-17-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-17.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you&#8217;re looking for a £4.5m defender who can simply get on with the job, Luke Shaw is one of the safest places to start. He started all 38 Premier League games last season, a remarkable record given his previous struggles with fitness, and Michael Carrick&#8217;s faith in him is clearly evident. Unless United bring in another left-back, Shaw looks well placed to continue as a regular.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There is plenty to like about the team context too. Manchester United had the third-best expected goals conceded (xGC) in the league last season, behind only Arsenal and Liverpool, and they couldn&#8217;t have wished for a better opening: Hull (A) and Ipswich (H) in the first two Gameweeks. Shaw is also currently United&#8217;s second-most-owned player after Bruno Fernandes.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At £4.5m, therefore, Shaw is a very straightforward proposition: regular minutes, a strong defence and excellent opening fixtures. His fitness will obviously need monitoring after his recent knock, but if he is fit and United don&#8217;t add another left-back, he looks like a very useful budget enabler.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">However, I have a slightly different view if you can find an extra £0.5m.</p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Fantasy Football Hub(FFHUB)</mark></a></strong></p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full is-resized"><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1000" height="596" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_MoneyBack_1000x596.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84100" style="width:768px;height:undefinedpx" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_MoneyBack_1000x596.png 1000w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_MoneyBack_1000x596-300x179.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_MoneyBack_1000x596-768x458.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/AAFPL_MoneyBack_1000x596-600x358.png 600w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px" /></a><figcaption class="wp-element-caption"><strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Fantasy Football Hub</mark></a></strong> is a high-quality FPL website offering a wide range of FPL content, tools, data, planners, and more. Memberships are available for the 2026/27 season at a <strong><a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl"><mark><mark style="background-color:#ffffff" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">50% discount</mark></mark></a></strong> along with a win-your-mini-league or get-your-money-back guarantee<strong>(<a href="https://www.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/terms-and-conditions" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">T&amp;C Applicable</mark></a>).</strong> (Click on the image above to claim the offer)</figcaption></figure>
</div>


<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Harry Maguire (£5.0m) – DEF, Man Utd – 9.7% TSB</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-23-1024x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84731" style="width:664px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-23-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-23-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-23-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-23-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-23-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-23.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you can stretch to £5.0m, I&#8217;d rather have Maguire.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The numbers make a surprisingly strong case. Despite starting just 19 games last season compared with Shaw&#8217;s 38, Maguire returned 90 FPL points, while Shaw managed 113. On a per-start basis, that&#8217;s a very different story.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Maguire averaged 8.21 defensive contributions per 90, compared with Shaw&#8217;s 6.24, and offered considerably more attacking threat: 0.60 shots per 90 versus Shaw&#8217;s 0.17. In those 19 starts, Maguire registered 1 goal and 2 assists, while Shaw&#8217;s 38 starts produced just 1 goal and 1 assist.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The biggest difference could come from set pieces. Maguire is a considerably more imposing target at corners and has genuine goal threat from dead-ball situations, while his defensive contribution gives him another route to points. He also looked back to his best under Carrick last season, suggesting that his FPL potential isn&#8217;t purely theoretical.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The opening fixtures are identical, of course – Hull (A) and Ipswich (H) – and Maguire&#8217;s absence against Leeds in pre-season was simply load management rather than an injury concern.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">So, my verdict is fairly straightforward: Shaw is the better £4.5m enabler. Maguire is the better £5.0m defender.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you&#8217;re absolutely squeezing every penny to accommodate your premium attackers, Shaw makes perfect sense. But if you can find the extra £0.5m, I&#8217;d personally upgrade Shaw to Maguire. The combination of higher defensive involvement, greater set-piece threat and stronger attacking numbers makes that extra half-million look very well spent.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read: </strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/premier-league-penalty-set-piece-takers-2026-27-pl-season/"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Premier League Penalty &amp; Set Piece Takers | 2026/27 PL Season</mark></strong></a></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Trai Hume (£4.5m) – DEF, Sunderland – 4.8% TSB</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-24-1024x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84732" style="width:548px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-24-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-24-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-24-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-24-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-24-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-24.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Trai Hume is exactly the kind of player you want to discover when looking for a £4.5m defender: a defender who might not actually be defending much.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Hume was already a reliable starter last season, featuring 3,032 Premier League minutes across 34 starts and finishing with 110 FPL points, 2 goals, an assist and 9 Clean Sheets. But what has really pushed him onto the FPL radar is his role in pre-season. Hume has been deployed at right wing in each of his last four friendlies, rather than his usual right-back role, and has already produced a goal and an assist in that spell. He also scored against Lens while playing further forward.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">That positional change could be huge. A £4.5m defender playing as a winger gets access to considerably more attacking situations than your average budget defender, while still retaining the possibility of clean-sheet points. Hume&#8217;s numbers already hint at some attacking intent, with 34 shots and 87 crosses last season, and he has shown that he can contribute when pushed further forward.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The obvious caveat is that the winger position isn&#8217;t guaranteed. Sunderland are still looking for a natural right winger, and if they bring one in before the deadline, Hume could return to right-back. But if no signing arrives, he has a genuine chance of starting the season in an advanced role – and that makes him extremely difficult to ignore at £4.5m.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The fixtures make the punt even more appealing: Ipswich (A), Fulham (H) and Brentford (A) in the opening three Gameweeks.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At 4.8% ownership, Hume is already attracting attention, but I&#8217;m not ready to lock him into my GW1 team just yet. If he continues to start on the right wing, though, he could become one of the standout budget defenders of the season. This is definitely one to monitor right up until the deadline.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Further Read: </strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/08/best-fpl-forwards-at-each-price-point-for-the-2026-27-season/"><strong><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Best FPL Forwards at Each Price Point for the 2026/27 Season</mark></strong></a></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Neco Williams (£5.0m) – DEF, Nott&#8217;m Forest – 4.3% TSB</strong></h3>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-16-1024x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84724" style="width:652px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-16-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-16-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-16-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-16-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-16-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/202627-FPL-Pre-Season-16.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Neco Williams is one of the defenders I&#8217;m particularly interested in at £5.0m, and the reason goes beyond the usual clean-sheet potential. No defender registered more shots in the Premier League last season than Williams, with 46, while he finished with 2 goals, 3 assists and 9 Clean Sheets across the campaign. For a defender, that&#8217;s a very healthy attacking profile – and there could be considerably more to come this season.</p>



<h4 class="wp-block-heading">Top Defenders for Shots last season:</h4>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/top-10-shots-gw1-38-1024x768.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84733" style="width:717px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/top-10-shots-gw1-38-1024x768.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/top-10-shots-gw1-38-300x225.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/top-10-shots-gw1-38-768x576.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/top-10-shots-gw1-38-600x450.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/top-10-shots-gw1-38.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
