<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>All Stats below are from FFHUB. For more Stats, Player Comparison, Points Prediction, Rate My Team AI Tool, AI Recommended Transfers, FPL Planners and much more to improve your FPL Game &#8211; <a href="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl" data-type="link" data-id="https://go.fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/landing/money-back-26?utm_source=affiliate&amp;utm_medium=affiliates&amp;utm_campaign=allaboutfpl&amp;utm_content=money-back&amp;via=allaboutfpl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Subscribe now for the 2026/27 season with an exclusive 50% </mark></a><a href="https://fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/?via=allaboutfpl"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">off discount</mark></a> and with a win your mini-league or money-back guarantee!</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The arrival of Oliver Glasner is what really catches my eye. Based on what we&#8217;ve seen in pre-season, Williams could be used as a very advanced wing-back, potentially playing a role similar to the one Daniel Muñoz enjoyed under Glasner at Crystal Palace. Muñoz returned 142 FPL points from 37 starts in 2024/25 and another 136 from just 29 starts in 2025/26, demonstrating just how valuable Glasner&#8217;s system can be for an attack-minded defender. Williams has already been taking corners in pre-season too, while his 150 open-play crosses last season underline his willingness to get forward and deliver.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The fixtures make him even more appealing. Forest face Leeds (H) in GW1, followed by Spurs (H) and Coventry (H) within the first five Gameweeks. The GW1 fixture against Leeds is particularly attractive if you&#8217;re looking for an early attacking return, while his price also makes him an interesting option for managers considering a GW1 Bench Boost.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There is always some uncertainty when a new manager changes a team&#8217;s shape, but if Williams is indeed the beneficiary of Glasner&#8217;s system and operates as the high wing-back we&#8217;ve seen in pre-season, £5.0m could prove to be an absolute bargain. With DEFCON potential, attacking numbers and now the possibility of set-piece involvement, Williams has the profile of a defender who can score points at both ends of the pitch.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Neco Williams also rotates well with Van Ewijk(4.0 Coventry Defender) as highlighted in our <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/fpl-rotational-pairs-combinations-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/" data-type="link" data-id="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/fpl-rotational-pairs-combinations-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">FPL Rotational Pairs and Combinations article</mark></a></strong>. Van Ewijk covers up Williams&#8217;s tough fixtures vs Liverpool, Villa, Arsenal and Man City really well as seen below. </p>


