<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center">Conclusion and Key Points- FPL Team Structure</h2>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Importance of £6.0 Forward:</strong> You must plan to have at least one £6.0 Forward in your teams because that is the price point that allows you to &#8230;. Also, there are quite a lot of quality and reliable options in your £6.0 million price bracket &#8211; DCL, Igor Jesus, Solanke, Brobbey, whom you can swap around among them based on fixture runs.</li>
</ul>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-1-1024x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84637" style="width:572px;height:auto" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-1-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-1-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-1-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-1-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-1-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-1.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>BIG AT THE BACK is so back</strong>: £5.0-£5.5 Defenders are value for money compared to Midfielders in the same price point. </li>
</ul>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center">Impact of DEFCON- Defenders vs Budget Mids vs Budget Forwards Comparison:</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Most Points last season: (Included only Players &lt;= £6.5 this season)</strong></p>



<figure class="wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped wp-block-gallery-1 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" data-id="84638" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-1-1-1024x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84638" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-1-1-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-1-1-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-1-1-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-1-1-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-1-1-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-1-1.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" data-id="84639" src="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-2-1024x1024.png" alt="" class="wp-image-84639" srcset="https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-2-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-2-300x300.png 300w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-2-150x150.png 150w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-2-768x768.png 768w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-2-600x600.png 600w, https://cdn.allaboutfpl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Copy-of-202627-FPL-Pre-Season-2.png 1080w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Key Notes from the above data:</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Despite FPL increasing the prices of DEFCON DEFs &amp; MIDs, they are still excellent value for money. Think FPL got it spot on with Pricing this season</li>



<li>Guehi, Senesi(if nailed), VVD, Tarko are all fixture-proof &amp; good picks even though they are Premiums now</li>



<li>Playing 5 at the back is genuinely a good option as suggested by Player Count in Top 50 &#8211; GK(9), DEF(20), MID(18), FWD(3)</li>



<li>The 1st Forward in the above list comes only at 20th position(DCL)</li>



<li>As many as 11 DEFs make the Top 20 &amp; most of them are DEFCON guys</li>



<li>Raya at £6.0 is a good shout &amp; still a value pick</li>



<li>Garner(Currently injured), Anderson, Le Fee all might sound boring but will tick over through the season &amp; get the job done</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Other Key Notes and Team Structure Notes:</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>These are all important price points that allow flexibility around your Team Structure &#8211;<strong> One or two 7.5-8.5 MIDS, One or two 5.5 DEFs, One 5.5 MID, One 7.5 FWD. </strong></li>



<li><strong>Don&#8217;t go with NO</strong> <strong>BRUNO AND HAALAND</strong>&#8211; It is not advisable to go without both Bruno and Haaland. Even going without one of them is a riskier move in our opinion as it might be difficult to get them later. </li>



<li><strong>Planning for Isak/Saka/Palmer</strong>&#8211; Not Picking a Palmer/Saka and Isak is totally fine for GW1 but you should build and plan a team structure in such a way that you can get them easily later if needed. </li>



<li><strong>Lack of Mid-priced Forwards other than Joao Pedro/Cheap Forwards: </strong>This is what makes things interesting with no standout Forwards options at 5.5 or lower and not much competition for Pedro in the 7.5 price point. This makes Pedro almost close to a must own considering he has had a full and good pre-season as well. </li>



<li><strong>Rotating 4.5/5.0 Defenders </strong>is a legit option this season(Read more: <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/fpl-rotational-pairs-combinations-for-the-2026-27-fpl-season/" data-type="post" data-id="84016" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">Best FPL Rotational Pairs and Combinations for 2026/27 FPL Season</mark></a></strong>). Finding starting <strong><a href="https://allaboutfpl.com/2026/07/best-4-0-million-fpl-defenders-for-2026-27-fpl-season/" data-type="post" data-id="84145" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><mark style="background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)" class="has-inline-color has-vivid-red-color">4.0 million defenders</mark></a></strong> is also not difficult.</li>



<li><strong>Great value in £6.0 and less MID</strong>. There might be two penalty takers for Mid-table teams in Ndiaye and Le Fee. There are solid reliable 5.5 Million Midfielders in Sangare, Gross who must be very nailed and consistent as well. </li>



<li>There is <strong>no starting £4.5 Midfielder at the momen</strong>t (Eye on Slater &amp; Yates). So it is not advisable to go for a dead spot in midfield spoiling your flexibility. </li>



<li><strong>Team Structure 1 and Team Structure 3 </strong>are our favorites right now due to the flexibility it offers in terms of team structure, transfers and formations. </li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There is no right or wrong team in FPL. This is just a Team structure guide and more like an open conversation to understand the structures better. Play your own game. Hope this article was useful, Good luck for the season!</p>



